{"version":"https://jsonfeed.org/version/1.1","title":"Polestar","home_page_url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs","feed_url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs.json","items":[{"id":"a88b95c9-d324-4ce2-9ea6-9fe28a99eb95","title":"Salesforce Solution Architect","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/8319785-salesforce-solution-architect","date_published":"2026-09-04T08:46:23+02:00","content_html":"\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAt Polestar, you will have the opportunity to influence the future architecture of one of our most strategic commercial platforms, working at the intersection of customer experience, business transformation, and modern digital engineering.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePolestar is accelerating the transition to sustainable mobility through electric performance. Digital Commercial plays a critical role in enabling customer growth, customer experience, sales, fleet and retailer operations, digital channels, and commercial excellence across all markets.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSalesforce is a strategic platform within Polestar's digital landscape, supporting customer engagement, sales, fleet operations, customer service, marketing, portals, AI-enabled experiences, and critical integrations with enterprise platforms such as ERP, integration platforms, data platforms, and other digital products.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAs our business continues to evolve, we are strengthening our internal architecture capability and establishing clearer architectural ownership, standards, and governance across the Salesforce ecosystem. This role will help define the future direction of the platform, ensuring solutions remain scalable, secure, compliant, and aligned with Polestar's enterprise architecture.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThis position is located at Gothenburg, Sweden. We believe in a hybrid model when it comes to remote and onsite work, knowing that both in-person collaboration and individual time to focus are needed. What matters most is that people get the time, and support, to do what needs to be done. And to enjoy doing it, of course.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAs a Salesforce Solution Architect, you will provide architectural leadership across Polestar's Salesforce landscape, spanning Sales Cloud, Service Cloud, Experience Cloud, Marketing Cloud, Agentforce, customer portals, fleet solutions, and related integrations. You will work closely with product managers, business stakeholders, engineers, enterprise architects, and external partners to ensure that solutions are aligned with both business objectives and long-term technology strategy.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe role requires balancing customer experience, business process efficiency, integration complexity, security requirements, and platform sustainability. You will help teams make the right architectural decisions while reducing technical debt, increasing reuse, and enabling faster delivery across multiple products and markets. You will be a key contributor in defining platform guardrails, integration patterns, data ownership principles, and future-state architecture for one of Polestar's most business-critical platforms.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat you'll do\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eYou will lead solution architecture across multiple initiatives and help shape the evolution of Polestar's Salesforce ecosystem.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSee below for a more thorough breakdown of the various tasks and areas you'll be responsible for:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDesigning scalable Salesforce solutions across customer, sales, service, fleet, and commercial domains\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLeading solution architecture for strategic Salesforce initiatives and programmes\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDefining architecture standards, patterns, and guardrails for Salesforce development\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eEnsuring alignment with enterprise architecture principles and technology standards\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDriving integration architecture across Salesforce, AWS, ERP systems, customer identity, data platforms, and digital products\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDefining data ownership, master data, and information flow principles\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSupporting product teams in architecture decisions, technical design, and solution governance\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eEnsuring solutions meet security, privacy, compliance, and audit requirements\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eManaging cross-team dependencies and reducing solution complexity\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDriving platform scalability, maintainability, and operational excellence\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSupporting roadmap planning and target architecture definition\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eContributing to architecture reviews and governance forums\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMentoring engineers and supporting the broader architecture community\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn your daily work, you will collaborate with teams across CRM, Customer Experience, Sales, Fleet, Marketing, Customer Care, Data \u0026amp; AI, Enterprise Architecture, and Digital Commercial leadership. You will also work closely with enterprise architects, chief architects, solution architects, product teams, and strategic partners.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWho you are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eYou are comfortable navigating complex business domains and translating business needs into practical and sustainable Salesforce solutions. You can balance strategic thinking with hands-on architecture work and enjoy collaborating across business and technology teams. You have strong communication skills and can explain architectural concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences. You understand that great architecture is not just about technology. It is about enabling business outcomes while maintaining simplicity, governance, and long-term sustainability.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eTo be a great fit for this position, we believe you have:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMinimum 5 years of experience as a Solution Architect, Salesforce Architect, or Lead Salesforce Consultant\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDeep knowledge of Salesforce platform capabilities and architecture patterns\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience with Sales Cloud, Service Cloud, Experience Cloud, and Salesforce integrations\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience designing APIs, event-driven integrations, and distributed solutions\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong understanding of customer data management and enterprise integration patterns\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience working with cloud-native architectures and modern development practices\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eKnowledge of security, privacy, identity, and compliance requirements\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience working in agile product organisations\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAbility to lead architecture across multiple teams and business domains\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe following would be considered an advantage:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSalesforce certifications such as Application Architect, System Architect, or Certified Technical Architect (CTA)\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience with Marketing Cloud or Agentforce\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience integrating Salesforce with ERP, customer identity, and enterprise data platforms\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience within automotive, retail, mobility, or direct-to-consumer digital businesses\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePolestar is an international company, with various backgrounds represented. English, therefore, is the language of written and spoken communication. And though we have a global presence, we maintain the growth-mindset. Change happens often at Polestar. But so does progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs this you?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIf the above matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. Our selection process is ongoing, and the job advert will remain open until it's filled.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Salesforce Solution Architect","description":"\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAt Polestar, you will have the opportunity to influence the future architecture of one of our most strategic commercial platforms, working at the intersection of customer experience, business transformation, and modern digital engineering.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePolestar is accelerating the transition to sustainable mobility through electric performance. Digital Commercial plays a critical role in enabling customer growth, customer experience, sales, fleet and retailer operations, digital channels, and commercial excellence across all markets.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSalesforce is a strategic platform within Polestar's digital landscape, supporting customer engagement, sales, fleet operations, customer service, marketing, portals, AI-enabled experiences, and critical integrations with enterprise platforms such as ERP, integration platforms, data platforms, and other digital products.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAs our business continues to evolve, we are strengthening our internal architecture capability and establishing clearer architectural ownership, standards, and governance across the Salesforce ecosystem. This role will help define the future direction of the platform, ensuring solutions remain scalable, secure, compliant, and aligned with Polestar's enterprise architecture.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThis position is located at Gothenburg, Sweden. We believe in a hybrid model when it comes to remote and onsite work, knowing that both in-person collaboration and individual time to focus are needed. What matters most is that people get the time, and support, to do what needs to be done. And to enjoy doing it, of course.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAs a Salesforce Solution Architect, you will provide architectural leadership across Polestar's Salesforce landscape, spanning Sales Cloud, Service Cloud, Experience Cloud, Marketing Cloud, Agentforce, customer portals, fleet solutions, and related integrations. You will work closely with product managers, business stakeholders, engineers, enterprise architects, and external partners to ensure that solutions are aligned with both business objectives and long-term technology strategy.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe role requires balancing customer experience, business process efficiency, integration complexity, security requirements, and platform sustainability. You will help teams make the right architectural decisions while reducing technical debt, increasing reuse, and enabling faster delivery across multiple products and markets. You will be a key contributor in defining platform guardrails, integration patterns, data ownership principles, and future-state architecture for one of Polestar's most business-critical platforms.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat you'll do\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eYou will lead solution architecture across multiple initiatives and help shape the evolution of Polestar's Salesforce ecosystem.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSee below for a more thorough breakdown of the various tasks and areas you'll be responsible for:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDesigning scalable Salesforce solutions across customer, sales, service, fleet, and commercial domains\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLeading solution architecture for strategic Salesforce initiatives and programmes\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDefining architecture standards, patterns, and guardrails for Salesforce development\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eEnsuring alignment with enterprise architecture principles and technology standards\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDriving integration architecture across Salesforce, AWS, ERP systems, customer identity, data platforms, and digital products\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDefining data ownership, master data, and information flow principles\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSupporting product teams in architecture decisions, technical design, and solution governance\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eEnsuring solutions meet security, privacy, compliance, and audit requirements\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eManaging cross-team dependencies and reducing solution complexity\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDriving platform scalability, maintainability, and operational excellence\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSupporting roadmap planning and target architecture definition\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eContributing to architecture reviews and governance forums\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMentoring engineers and supporting the broader architecture community\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn your daily work, you will collaborate with teams across CRM, Customer Experience, Sales, Fleet, Marketing, Customer Care, Data \u0026amp; AI, Enterprise Architecture, and Digital Commercial leadership. You will also work closely with enterprise architects, chief architects, solution architects, product teams, and strategic partners.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWho you are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eYou are comfortable navigating complex business domains and translating business needs into practical and sustainable Salesforce solutions. You can balance strategic thinking with hands-on architecture work and enjoy collaborating across business and technology teams. You have strong communication skills and can explain architectural concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences. You understand that great architecture is not just about technology. It is about enabling business outcomes while maintaining simplicity, governance, and long-term sustainability.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eTo be a great fit for this position, we believe you have:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMinimum 5 years of experience as a Solution Architect, Salesforce Architect, or Lead Salesforce Consultant\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDeep knowledge of Salesforce platform capabilities and architecture patterns\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience with Sales Cloud, Service Cloud, Experience Cloud, and Salesforce integrations\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience designing APIs, event-driven integrations, and distributed solutions\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong understanding of customer data management and enterprise integration patterns\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience working with cloud-native architectures and modern development practices\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eKnowledge of security, privacy, identity, and compliance requirements\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience working in agile product organisations\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAbility to lead architecture across multiple teams and business domains\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe following would be considered an advantage:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSalesforce certifications such as Application Architect, System Architect, or Certified Technical Architect (CTA)\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience with Marketing Cloud or Agentforce\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience integrating Salesforce with ERP, customer identity, and enterprise data platforms\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience within automotive, retail, mobility, or direct-to-consumer digital businesses\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePolestar is an international company, with various backgrounds represented. English, therefore, is the language of written and spoken communication. And though we have a global presence, we maintain the growth-mindset. Change happens often at Polestar. But so does progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs this you?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIf the above matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. Our selection process is ongoing, and the job advert will remain open until it's filled.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":8319785},"datePosted":"2026-09-04T08:46:23+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Assar Gabrielssons väg 9","addressLocality":"Göteborg","postalCode":"418 78","addressCountry":"SE","addressRegion":"Nordics \u0026 UK"}}]}},{"id":"26a1bf5d-aa8e-4521-aa9c-93b950c7b433","title":"User Insights Leader","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/8307301-user-insights-leader","date_published":"2026-09-02T09:33:42+02:00","content_html":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWe're currently looking for a \u003cstrong\u003eUser Insights Leader\u003c/strong\u003e. Someone to join our \u003cstrong\u003eConcepts \u0026amp; Simulation \u003c/strong\u003eteam, which is a part of the Attributes \u0026amp; Validation team in shaping and advancing the next generation of the Polestar user experience. Someone with a passion for understanding customer needs, translating insights into impactful experiences, and driving innovation at the intersection of technology, design, and human behaviour.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePolestar user experience development is entering a new phase focused on technology, functionality, and user satisfaction. We're investing in the next generation of the Polestar interface through streamlined everyday user journeys, deeper integration of AI-enabled experiences, and the technical foundations needed to support innovative and intuitive solutions.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWorking at the center of UX, you'll combine user research, behavioural insights, customer data, and cross-functional collaboration to influence product direction and create experiences that are both desirable and easy to use. You'll play a key role in balancing customer needs, business objectives, and technical possibilities while helping shape the future of mobility.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThis position is located at the Polestar headquarters in Gothenburg. We believe in a hybrid model when it comes to remote and onsite work, knowing that both in-person collaboration and individual time to focus are needed. What matters most is that people get the time, and support, to do what needs to be done. And to enjoy doing it, of course.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe responsibilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eIn this role, you'll be expected to drive and structure complex Product User Experience initiatives while ensuring alignment across multiple functions and stakeholders. Working as a member of the Concepts \u0026amp; Simulation team, you'll be instrumental in defining user journeys, establishing interaction principles, and supporting the development of intuitive and seamless customer experiences.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eSee below for a more thorough breakdown of the various tasks and areas you'll be responsible for:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eLead and structure complex Product User Experience initiatives, defining user journeys, interaction principles, and use cases that create intuitive and seamless customer experiences.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eAct as a cross-functional project lead, collaborating with Product, Design, Engineering, Customer Experience, Procurement, and external partners to drive alignment and delivery.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eDefine and maintain UX requirements at system, hardware, and software levels while co-creating UX solutions across product development teams.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eEstablish and manage UX evaluation methodologies, including usability assessments, customer satisfaction measurements, benchmarking, and comparative scoreboards.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eDrive data-informed UX development by coordinating user research activities, leveraging customer insights, and identifying opportunities to improve product experiences.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe ideal candidate\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eIn order to succeed in this role, and at Polestar in general, there are a few characteristics you'll need to have. Tenacity. Flexibility. Curiosity. The ability to take the initiative, to meet deadlines and requirements, and to abandon ideas when they're not feasible.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eWe're looking for someone who combines strategic thinking with hands-on execution and who thrives when working across functions to solve complex customer experience challenges.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIn addition, you'll need the following qualifications:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eBSc or MSc in Mechanical Engineering, Product Development, User Experience or equivalent\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eProven experience leading complex cross-functional projects within product development, balancing both strategic and operational responsibilities.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong expertise in UX principles, user journey mapping, interaction design methodologies, and customer-centric product development.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience developing evaluation frameworks, benchmarking methodologies, and translating customer insights into actionable product improvements.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExcellent communication, stakeholder management, and analytical skills, with the ability to influence decisions across a broad range of stakeholders.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eAbility to influence and align stakeholders across multiple functions and organizational levels.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStakeholder interfaces\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eIn this role, you'll collaborate with a broad range of internal and external stakeholders, including:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eInternal\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eProduct Management\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eDesign\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eCustomer Experience\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eR\u0026amp;D\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eProcurement\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eAttribute Leaders\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eCross-functional Product Development Teams\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eExternal\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eVolvo Cars and stakeholders within the Geely Group\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eSuppliers and development partners\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eUser research and customer insight partners\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePolestar is an international company, with various backgrounds represented. English, therefore, is the language of written and spoken communication. And though we have a global presence, we maintain the growth mindset. Change happens often at Polestar. But so does progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIf the above matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. Our selection process is ongoing, and the job advert will remain open until it's filled.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"User Insights Leader","description":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWe're currently looking for a \u003cstrong\u003eUser Insights Leader\u003c/strong\u003e. Someone to join our \u003cstrong\u003eConcepts \u0026amp; Simulation \u003c/strong\u003eteam, which is a part of the Attributes \u0026amp; Validation team in shaping and advancing the next generation of the Polestar user experience. Someone with a passion for understanding customer needs, translating insights into impactful experiences, and driving innovation at the intersection of technology, design, and human behaviour.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePolestar user experience development is entering a new phase focused on technology, functionality, and user satisfaction. We're investing in the next generation of the Polestar interface through streamlined everyday user journeys, deeper integration of AI-enabled experiences, and the technical foundations needed to support innovative and intuitive solutions.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWorking at the center of UX, you'll combine user research, behavioural insights, customer data, and cross-functional collaboration to influence product direction and create experiences that are both desirable and easy to use. You'll play a key role in balancing customer needs, business objectives, and technical possibilities while helping shape the future of mobility.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThis position is located at the Polestar headquarters in Gothenburg. We believe in a hybrid model when it comes to remote and onsite work, knowing that both in-person collaboration and individual time to focus are needed. What matters most is that people get the time, and support, to do what needs to be done. And to enjoy doing it, of course.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe responsibilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eIn this role, you'll be expected to drive and structure complex Product User Experience initiatives while ensuring alignment across multiple functions and stakeholders. Working as a member of the Concepts \u0026amp; Simulation team, you'll be instrumental in defining user journeys, establishing interaction principles, and supporting the development of intuitive and seamless customer experiences.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eSee below for a more thorough breakdown of the various tasks and areas you'll be responsible for:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eLead and structure complex Product User Experience initiatives, defining user journeys, interaction principles, and use cases that create intuitive and seamless customer experiences.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eAct as a cross-functional project lead, collaborating with Product, Design, Engineering, Customer Experience, Procurement, and external partners to drive alignment and delivery.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eDefine and maintain UX requirements at system, hardware, and software levels while co-creating UX solutions across product development teams.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eEstablish and manage UX evaluation methodologies, including usability assessments, customer satisfaction measurements, benchmarking, and comparative scoreboards.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eDrive data-informed UX development by coordinating user research activities, leveraging customer insights, and identifying opportunities to improve product experiences.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe ideal candidate\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eIn order to succeed in this role, and at Polestar in general, there are a few characteristics you'll need to have. Tenacity. Flexibility. Curiosity. The ability to take the initiative, to meet deadlines and requirements, and to abandon ideas when they're not feasible.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eWe're looking for someone who combines strategic thinking with hands-on execution and who thrives when working across functions to solve complex customer experience challenges.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIn addition, you'll need the following qualifications:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eBSc or MSc in Mechanical Engineering, Product Development, User Experience or equivalent\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eProven experience leading complex cross-functional projects within product development, balancing both strategic and operational responsibilities.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong expertise in UX principles, user journey mapping, interaction design methodologies, and customer-centric product development.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience developing evaluation frameworks, benchmarking methodologies, and translating customer insights into actionable product improvements.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExcellent communication, stakeholder management, and analytical skills, with the ability to influence decisions across a broad range of stakeholders.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eAbility to influence and align stakeholders across multiple functions and organizational levels.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStakeholder interfaces\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eIn this role, you'll collaborate with a broad range of internal and external stakeholders, including:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eInternal\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eProduct Management\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eDesign\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eCustomer Experience\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eR\u0026amp;D\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eProcurement\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eAttribute Leaders\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eCross-functional Product Development Teams\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eExternal\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eVolvo Cars and stakeholders within the Geely Group\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eSuppliers and development partners\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eUser research and customer insight partners\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePolestar is an international company, with various backgrounds represented. English, therefore, is the language of written and spoken communication. And though we have a global presence, we maintain the growth mindset. Change happens often at Polestar. But so does progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIf the above matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. Our selection process is ongoing, and the job advert will remain open until it's filled.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":8307301},"datePosted":"2026-09-02T09:33:42+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Assar Gabrielssons väg 9","addressLocality":"Göteborg","postalCode":"418 78","addressCountry":"SE","addressRegion":"Nordics \u0026 UK"}}]}},{"id":"cdbc837d-0879-486d-9425-11d5a1b34239","title":"Compensation \u0026 Benefits Specialist","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/8303004-compensation-benefits-specialist","date_published":"2026-09-01T15:13:11+02:00","content_html":"\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWe're currently looking for a Compensation \u0026amp; Benefits Specialist for a 14-month fixed-term contract, covering parental leave. If you're driven by making a real impact, take pride in providing high-quality support, and thrive on creating value for the business, this could be your next step. You’ll be part of a small, agile team and report to the Global Head of Compensation \u0026amp; Benefits. The team plays an important role in shaping fair, competitive, and compliant reward practices across Polestar. From merit review and bonus processes to pay transparency and pay equity, job architecture, job evaluation, incentive programs, international assignments, and benefits governance, the team partners closely with HR and both internal and external stakeholders.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThis position is located at our Global Headquarters in Gothenburg, Sweden. We embrace a hybrid working model, recognizing the value of both in-person collaboration and focused remote work. What matters most is having the time, tools, trust, and support to get things done, and to enjoy doing them.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe responsibilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn this role, you'll be a part of driving important Compensation \u0026amp; Benefits initiatives, including Pay Transparency, Pay Equity, Job Architecture, and the global Merit Review process. You'll be a trusted partner to HR and business leaders on all Compensation \u0026amp; Benefits matters, helping us design and deliver practices that support the attraction, retention, and motivation of talent across markets. You'll work on both Sweden-specific topics and global projects, combining strategic initiatives with hands-on operational delivery. See below for a more thorough breakdown of the various tasks and areas you'll be responsible for:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLead initiatives related to Pay Transparency and Pay Equity.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eBe a part of developing and maintaining our Job Architecture, including position evaluations, market benchmarking, salary range development, and role calibration.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eProvide subject matter expertise and guidance in Compensation \u0026amp; Benefits, including communication and training for managers and employees.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDrive and contribute to local and global C\u0026amp;B projects, including share-based incentive programs, international assignments, policy updates, vendor relationships, and regulatory compliance.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSupport Global Mobility processes, including international local hires and expat assignments, work permits, tax-related coordination, payroll input, and collaboration with external vendors.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDevelop and maintain compensation structures and benchmarks to ensure competitive, fair, and business-relevant reward practices across markets.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePerform gender pay gap and pay equity analysis, identifying trends, risks, and actions to support transparent and compliant compensation practices.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eParticipate in merit review activities, including planning, data preparation, stakeholder support, process coordination, and follow-up to ensure a fair and well-executed annual review.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe ideal candidate\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn order to succeed in this role, and at Polestar in general, you'll need to be proactive, adaptable, and detail-oriented. You take ownership, meet deadlines, and are not afraid to pivot when needed. You are equally comfortable contributing to strategic initiatives and handling hands-on operational tasks.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eYou have a structured and analytical way of working, with the ability to turn data into clear recommendations and practical solutions. Since this role involves close collaboration with HR, managers, employees, unions, external vendors, and authorities, strong communication skills and the ability to explain complex topics in a clear and professional way will be important. You can work independently with sensitive information, while also thriving in a team setting and in an international environment where priorities can shift and collaboration across countries and cultures is part of everyday work.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn addition, you'll need the following qualifications:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eA bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Finance, or a related field.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAt least three years of experience within Compensation \u0026amp; Benefits, preferably in a specialist role.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong knowledge of compensation frameworks, benefits programs, job evaluation methodologies, market benchmarking, and reward processes.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience working with HRIS systems, preferably Workday, compensation analytics tools, and advanced Excel.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong analytical, problem-solving, written and verbal communication skills, with discretion when handling confidential information and experience working across multiple countries and cultures.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePolestar is an international company, with various backgrounds represented. English, therefore, is the language of written and spoken communication. And though we have a global presence, we maintain the growth-mindset. Change happens often at Polestar. But so does progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIf the above matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. Our selection process is ongoing, and the job advert will remain open until it’s filled.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Compensation \u0026 Benefits Specialist","description":"\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWe're currently looking for a Compensation \u0026amp; Benefits Specialist for a 14-month fixed-term contract, covering parental leave. If you're driven by making a real impact, take pride in providing high-quality support, and thrive on creating value for the business, this could be your next step. You’ll be part of a small, agile team and report to the Global Head of Compensation \u0026amp; Benefits. The team plays an important role in shaping fair, competitive, and compliant reward practices across Polestar. From merit review and bonus processes to pay transparency and pay equity, job architecture, job evaluation, incentive programs, international assignments, and benefits governance, the team partners closely with HR and both internal and external stakeholders.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThis position is located at our Global Headquarters in Gothenburg, Sweden. We embrace a hybrid working model, recognizing the value of both in-person collaboration and focused remote work. What matters most is having the time, tools, trust, and support to get things done, and to enjoy doing them.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe responsibilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn this role, you'll be a part of driving important Compensation \u0026amp; Benefits initiatives, including Pay Transparency, Pay Equity, Job Architecture, and the global Merit Review process. You'll be a trusted partner to HR and business leaders on all Compensation \u0026amp; Benefits matters, helping us design and deliver practices that support the attraction, retention, and motivation of talent across markets. You'll work on both Sweden-specific topics and global projects, combining strategic initiatives with hands-on operational delivery. See below for a more thorough breakdown of the various tasks and areas you'll be responsible for:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLead initiatives related to Pay Transparency and Pay Equity.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eBe a part of developing and maintaining our Job Architecture, including position evaluations, market benchmarking, salary range development, and role calibration.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eProvide subject matter expertise and guidance in Compensation \u0026amp; Benefits, including communication and training for managers and employees.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDrive and contribute to local and global C\u0026amp;B projects, including share-based incentive programs, international assignments, policy updates, vendor relationships, and regulatory compliance.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSupport Global Mobility processes, including international local hires and expat assignments, work permits, tax-related coordination, payroll input, and collaboration with external vendors.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDevelop and maintain compensation structures and benchmarks to ensure competitive, fair, and business-relevant reward practices across markets.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePerform gender pay gap and pay equity analysis, identifying trends, risks, and actions to support transparent and compliant compensation practices.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eParticipate in merit review activities, including planning, data preparation, stakeholder support, process coordination, and follow-up to ensure a fair and well-executed annual review.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe ideal candidate\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn order to succeed in this role, and at Polestar in general, you'll need to be proactive, adaptable, and detail-oriented. You take ownership, meet deadlines, and are not afraid to pivot when needed. You are equally comfortable contributing to strategic initiatives and handling hands-on operational tasks.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eYou have a structured and analytical way of working, with the ability to turn data into clear recommendations and practical solutions. Since this role involves close collaboration with HR, managers, employees, unions, external vendors, and authorities, strong communication skills and the ability to explain complex topics in a clear and professional way will be important. You can work independently with sensitive information, while also thriving in a team setting and in an international environment where priorities can shift and collaboration across countries and cultures is part of everyday work.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn addition, you'll need the following qualifications:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eA bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Finance, or a related field.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAt least three years of experience within Compensation \u0026amp; Benefits, preferably in a specialist role.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong knowledge of compensation frameworks, benefits programs, job evaluation methodologies, market benchmarking, and reward processes.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience working with HRIS systems, preferably Workday, compensation analytics tools, and advanced Excel.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong analytical, problem-solving, written and verbal communication skills, with discretion when handling confidential information and experience working across multiple countries and cultures.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePolestar is an international company, with various backgrounds represented. English, therefore, is the language of written and spoken communication. And though we have a global presence, we maintain the growth-mindset. Change happens often at Polestar. But so does progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIf the above matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. Our selection process is ongoing, and the job advert will remain open until it’s filled.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":8303004},"datePosted":"2026-09-01T15:13:11+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Assar Gabrielssons väg 9","addressLocality":"Göteborg","postalCode":"418 78","addressCountry":"SE","addressRegion":"Nordics \u0026 UK"}}]}},{"id":"130b6986-94c2-41be-9cf6-09e026c64077","title":"Range \u0026 Performance Data Analyst","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/8291869-range-performance-data-analyst","date_published":"2026-08-31T13:44:56+02:00","content_html":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWe're currently looking for a \u003cstrong\u003eRange \u0026amp; Performance Data Analyst\u003c/strong\u003e. Someone to join our \u003cstrong\u003eConcepts \u0026amp; Simulation \u003c/strong\u003eteam, which is a part of the Attributes \u0026amp; Validation\u003cstrong\u003e team\u003c/strong\u003e in Engineering. supporting the development, validation, and optimization of vehicle range and performance through data-driven analysis and simulation.\u003c/span\u003e Someone with a passion for electric mobility, an interest in technology, and a desire to create the change we know is needed. And someone who doesn't mind the occasional bit of sustainable travel in the service of a cleaner form of electric performance.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe Concepts \u0026amp; Simulation team is responsible for supporting vehicle development with simulation and data analysis, ensuring our products deliver competitive range, energy efficiency, and performance. Working cross-functionally with engineering, quality, and homologation teams, we contribute to both current model year improvements and future vehicle programs.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis position is located at our\u003cspan\u003e headquarters in Gothenburg. \u003c/span\u003eWe believe in a hybrid model when it comes to remote and onsite work, knowing that both in-person collaboration and individual time to focus are needed. What matters most is that people get the time, and support, to do what needs to be done. And to enjoy doing it, of course.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe responsibilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn this role, you'll be expected to \u003cspan\u003esupport the development and validation of vehicle range and performance through advanced data analysis and simulation activities. Working as a member of the Concepts \u0026amp; Simulation team, you'll be instrumental in providing data-driven insights that influence engineering decisions, model year upgrades, and future vehicle programs.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eOwn and develop the data analysis activities related to Polestar's in-house Vehicle System Simulation tool, Pandora, including tool validation and simulation result assessments.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAnalyze, interpret, and present simulation results to support vehicle range, performance, model year upgrades, and future vehicle programs.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eCollaborate cross-functionally with CAE engineers, quality teams, and other R\u0026amp;D stakeholders to drive alignment and support development activities.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSupport homologation and pre-homologation testing through simulation, analysis, and technical recommendations.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eCoordinate activities with internal stakeholders and external engineering partners, including leading investigations and task force activities related to vehicle range and performance.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe ideal candidate\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn order to succeed in this role, and at Polestar in general, there are a few characteristics you'll need to have. Tenacity. Flexibility. Curiosity. The ability to take the initiative, to meet deadlines and requirements, and to abandon ideas when they're not feasible.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCompetences\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eBSc or MSc in Mechanical Engineering, preferably within Product Development, Automotive Engineering, or equivalent experience.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMinimum 5 years of experience within vehicle performance, simulation, CAE, data analysis, or a related automotive engineering field.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong technical knowledge of vehicle systems together with proven analytical and problem-solving capabilities.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eProficiency in MATLAB and Simulink, with coding and scripting experience used for simulation, analysis, and workflow automation.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong communication and stakeholder management skills, with experience working effectively across cross-functional engineering teams.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStakeholder interfaces\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn this role, you'll work cross-functionally with a variety of internal and external stakeholders, including:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSimulation Engineers across Polestar R\u0026amp;D.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eCMQ Quality teams.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eVehicle Range \u0026amp; Performance colleagues.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eHomologation and certification teams.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eEngineering suppliers and development partners.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eProgram and vehicle development teams\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is an international company, with various backgrounds represented. English, therefore, is the language of written and spoken communication. And though we have a global presence, we maintain the growth-mindset. Change happens often at Polestar. But so does progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf the above matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. Our selection process is ongoing, and the job advert will remain open until it’s filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Range \u0026 Performance Data Analyst","description":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWe're currently looking for a \u003cstrong\u003eRange \u0026amp; Performance Data Analyst\u003c/strong\u003e. Someone to join our \u003cstrong\u003eConcepts \u0026amp; Simulation \u003c/strong\u003eteam, which is a part of the Attributes \u0026amp; Validation\u003cstrong\u003e team\u003c/strong\u003e in Engineering. supporting the development, validation, and optimization of vehicle range and performance through data-driven analysis and simulation.\u003c/span\u003e Someone with a passion for electric mobility, an interest in technology, and a desire to create the change we know is needed. And someone who doesn't mind the occasional bit of sustainable travel in the service of a cleaner form of electric performance.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe Concepts \u0026amp; Simulation team is responsible for supporting vehicle development with simulation and data analysis, ensuring our products deliver competitive range, energy efficiency, and performance. Working cross-functionally with engineering, quality, and homologation teams, we contribute to both current model year improvements and future vehicle programs.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis position is located at our\u003cspan\u003e headquarters in Gothenburg. \u003c/span\u003eWe believe in a hybrid model when it comes to remote and onsite work, knowing that both in-person collaboration and individual time to focus are needed. What matters most is that people get the time, and support, to do what needs to be done. And to enjoy doing it, of course.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe responsibilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn this role, you'll be expected to \u003cspan\u003esupport the development and validation of vehicle range and performance through advanced data analysis and simulation activities. Working as a member of the Concepts \u0026amp; Simulation team, you'll be instrumental in providing data-driven insights that influence engineering decisions, model year upgrades, and future vehicle programs.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eOwn and develop the data analysis activities related to Polestar's in-house Vehicle System Simulation tool, Pandora, including tool validation and simulation result assessments.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAnalyze, interpret, and present simulation results to support vehicle range, performance, model year upgrades, and future vehicle programs.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eCollaborate cross-functionally with CAE engineers, quality teams, and other R\u0026amp;D stakeholders to drive alignment and support development activities.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSupport homologation and pre-homologation testing through simulation, analysis, and technical recommendations.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eCoordinate activities with internal stakeholders and external engineering partners, including leading investigations and task force activities related to vehicle range and performance.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe ideal candidate\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn order to succeed in this role, and at Polestar in general, there are a few characteristics you'll need to have. Tenacity. Flexibility. Curiosity. The ability to take the initiative, to meet deadlines and requirements, and to abandon ideas when they're not feasible.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCompetences\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eBSc or MSc in Mechanical Engineering, preferably within Product Development, Automotive Engineering, or equivalent experience.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMinimum 5 years of experience within vehicle performance, simulation, CAE, data analysis, or a related automotive engineering field.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong technical knowledge of vehicle systems together with proven analytical and problem-solving capabilities.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eProficiency in MATLAB and Simulink, with coding and scripting experience used for simulation, analysis, and workflow automation.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong communication and stakeholder management skills, with experience working effectively across cross-functional engineering teams.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStakeholder interfaces\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn this role, you'll work cross-functionally with a variety of internal and external stakeholders, including:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSimulation Engineers across Polestar R\u0026amp;D.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eCMQ Quality teams.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eVehicle Range \u0026amp; Performance colleagues.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eHomologation and certification teams.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eEngineering suppliers and development partners.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eProgram and vehicle development teams\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is an international company, with various backgrounds represented. English, therefore, is the language of written and spoken communication. And though we have a global presence, we maintain the growth-mindset. Change happens often at Polestar. But so does progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf the above matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. Our selection process is ongoing, and the job advert will remain open until it’s filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":8291869},"datePosted":"2026-08-31T13:44:56+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Assar Gabrielssons väg 9","addressLocality":"Göteborg","postalCode":"418 78","addressCountry":"SE","addressRegion":"Nordics \u0026 UK"}}]}},{"id":"dac5d07a-41b4-4c04-98b9-1cd068c77205","title":"HR Projects Admin (Fixed-Term Contract- 6 Months)","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/8284793-hr-projects-admin-fixed-term-contract-6-months","date_published":"2026-08-28T11:06:27+02:00","content_html":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe're currently looking for an HR Projects (FTC- 6 Months) to join our HR Business Commercial team and help us deliver agile and reliable HR support across the UK Sales Unit. This role is primarily focused on supporting a key HR data and systems project, ensuring employee data is accurate, complete and up to date within our HRIS and Employee Communication portal. The role will also provide HR administrative support and assist with wider HR activities as required. If you're passionate about attention to detail, data accuracy, continuous improvement and creating efficient HR processes, this is your chance to make an impact in a fast-moving, innovative environment.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou'll be part of the HR Business Commercial team and report to the HR Business Partner UK. The role is based in Bicester, UK. We recognize the value of in-person collaboration and have a 3 days a week in the office policy, but what matters most is having the time, tools and trust to get things done and to enjoy doing them.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePlease note that this is a six-month fixed-term position and, internally, the role will be known as HR Trainee. The role has been created to support a number of HR projects and organisational improvement initiatives during a period of increased business activity. This is a temporary position established to meet a specific business requirement and is therefore expected to end upon completion of the six-month fixed-term contract.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe responsibilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs an HR Projects Officer, you will play a key role in supporting critical HR system and data management activities, with a primary focus on ensuring employee data within our HRIS and employee communication portable is accurate, up to date, complete and maintained to a high standard. Working closely with the HR Business Partner UK, you will support HR projects, maintain data integrity, provide HR administrative support and assist with a variety of people-related activities across the business.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eKey Responsibilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Maintain, validate and cleanse employee data within our HRIS, ensuring accuracy, completeness and data integrity.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Drive the transfer and maintenance of employee data and documentation within our HRIS, ensuring all employee lifecycle records and documentation are captured and stored appropriately.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Review and optimise employee lifecycle processes within our HRIS, ensuring workflows remain effective, compliant and fit for purpose.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Maintain and update employee-facing HR information and communication portal, ensuring content remains relevant, accurate and accessible.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Produce HR reports, metrics and data analysis from the HRIS to support HR and business decision-making.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Support HR audits, compliance activities and governance requirements through effective record management and data controls.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Work closely with managers and stakeholders to ensure employee information is maintained accurately and consistently across HR systems.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Build effective working relationships across the business and contribute to continuous improvement initiatives.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Provide ad hoc HR administration and operational support across the HR team as required.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAbout You\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTo be successful in this role, you will be highly organised, detail-oriented and comfortable working with large volumes of employee data. You will enjoy problem-solving, have excellent attention to detail and be confident working with HR systems and multiple stakeholders. You will also be flexible and willing to support broader HR activities when required.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSkills, Experience \u0026amp; Qualifications\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Previous experience in an HR Administration, HR Coordinator, HR Projects or similar support role.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Experience maintaining employee data and working with HR systems.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Strong understanding of HR administration and employee lifecycle processes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Experience using Workday is highly desirable.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Candidates without Workday experience must have experience using another HR Information System (HRIS).\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Experience working with employee data, reporting and data accuracy initiatives.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Strong IT skills, particularly Microsoft Excel, PowerPoint and Microsoft Office applications.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Exceptional attention to detail and accuracy, combined with a proactive mindset and a commitment to delivering high-quality outcomes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Strong organisational and time-management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Excellent written and verbal communication skills.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Ability to handle confidential and sensitive information with discretion and professionalism.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Strong stakeholder management and relationship-building skills.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Ability to work effectively in a dynamic and changing environment.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is an international company with diverse backgrounds represented. English is our common language, and change happens often here, so does progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment where your work truly matters.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf this sounds like your next step, apply today. Our selection process is ongoing and the advert will remain open until the position is filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"HR Projects Admin (Fixed-Term Contract- 6 Months)","description":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe're currently looking for an HR Projects (FTC- 6 Months) to join our HR Business Commercial team and help us deliver agile and reliable HR support across the UK Sales Unit. This role is primarily focused on supporting a key HR data and systems project, ensuring employee data is accurate, complete and up to date within our HRIS and Employee Communication portal. The role will also provide HR administrative support and assist with wider HR activities as required. If you're passionate about attention to detail, data accuracy, continuous improvement and creating efficient HR processes, this is your chance to make an impact in a fast-moving, innovative environment.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou'll be part of the HR Business Commercial team and report to the HR Business Partner UK. The role is based in Bicester, UK. We recognize the value of in-person collaboration and have a 3 days a week in the office policy, but what matters most is having the time, tools and trust to get things done and to enjoy doing them.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePlease note that this is a six-month fixed-term position and, internally, the role will be known as HR Trainee. The role has been created to support a number of HR projects and organisational improvement initiatives during a period of increased business activity. This is a temporary position established to meet a specific business requirement and is therefore expected to end upon completion of the six-month fixed-term contract.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe responsibilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs an HR Projects Officer, you will play a key role in supporting critical HR system and data management activities, with a primary focus on ensuring employee data within our HRIS and employee communication portable is accurate, up to date, complete and maintained to a high standard. Working closely with the HR Business Partner UK, you will support HR projects, maintain data integrity, provide HR administrative support and assist with a variety of people-related activities across the business.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eKey Responsibilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Maintain, validate and cleanse employee data within our HRIS, ensuring accuracy, completeness and data integrity.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Drive the transfer and maintenance of employee data and documentation within our HRIS, ensuring all employee lifecycle records and documentation are captured and stored appropriately.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Review and optimise employee lifecycle processes within our HRIS, ensuring workflows remain effective, compliant and fit for purpose.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Maintain and update employee-facing HR information and communication portal, ensuring content remains relevant, accurate and accessible.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Produce HR reports, metrics and data analysis from the HRIS to support HR and business decision-making.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Support HR audits, compliance activities and governance requirements through effective record management and data controls.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Work closely with managers and stakeholders to ensure employee information is maintained accurately and consistently across HR systems.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Build effective working relationships across the business and contribute to continuous improvement initiatives.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Provide ad hoc HR administration and operational support across the HR team as required.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAbout You\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTo be successful in this role, you will be highly organised, detail-oriented and comfortable working with large volumes of employee data. You will enjoy problem-solving, have excellent attention to detail and be confident working with HR systems and multiple stakeholders. You will also be flexible and willing to support broader HR activities when required.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSkills, Experience \u0026amp; Qualifications\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Previous experience in an HR Administration, HR Coordinator, HR Projects or similar support role.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Experience maintaining employee data and working with HR systems.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Strong understanding of HR administration and employee lifecycle processes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Experience using Workday is highly desirable.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Candidates without Workday experience must have experience using another HR Information System (HRIS).\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Experience working with employee data, reporting and data accuracy initiatives.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Strong IT skills, particularly Microsoft Excel, PowerPoint and Microsoft Office applications.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Exceptional attention to detail and accuracy, combined with a proactive mindset and a commitment to delivering high-quality outcomes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Strong organisational and time-management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Excellent written and verbal communication skills.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Ability to handle confidential and sensitive information with discretion and professionalism.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Strong stakeholder management and relationship-building skills.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Ability to work effectively in a dynamic and changing environment.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is an international company with diverse backgrounds represented. English is our common language, and change happens often here, so does progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment where your work truly matters.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf this sounds like your next step, apply today. Our selection process is ongoing and the advert will remain open until the position is filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":8284793},"datePosted":"2026-08-28T11:06:27+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"OX27 8FY","addressLocality":"Bicester","postalCode":"OX27 8FY","addressCountry":"GB","addressRegion":"Nordics \u0026 UK"}}]}},{"id":"820b17a8-f627-4fbb-b033-75ddd74db873","title":"Cybersecurity Engineer","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/8260328-cybersecurity-engineer","date_published":"2026-08-24T00:00:00+02:00","content_html":"\u003ch4\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is accelerating the transition to sustainable mobility through electric performance. As a digital-first, cloud-driven organisation, cybersecurity is a critical enabler of our business, products, and services.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are looking for a Cybersecurity Engineer to strengthen and evolve our enterprise security capabilities. This role focuses on designing, implementing, operating, and continuously improving security controls that protect our workforce, data, identities, devices, networks, and digital services.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis is not a traditional operations-focused security role. We are looking for an engineer who enjoys building, automating, and improving security capabilities at scale while working closely with technology teams across the organisation.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs a Cybersecurity Engineer, you will play a key role in strengthening Polestar’s enterprise security posture and advancing our Zero Trust journey. You will help build scalable security capabilities that protect users, devices, identities, data, and enterprise services in a modern cloud-first environment.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis role is located at: \u003cstrong\u003ePolestar Headquarters, Gothenburg, Sweden.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe believe in empowerment and support flexible working hours and a hybrid way of working.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eWhat you’ll do\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will work across security engineering, automation, and operational resilience, partnering with teams throughout the organisation to embed security by design and continuously improve enterprise security capabilities.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis includes:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eImplementing and continuously improving security capabilities across endpoint, identity, network, collaboration, and data protection domains.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSupporting the deployment, optimisation, and governance of enterprise security platforms and controls.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eBuilding and maintaining security automations that reduce manual effort and improve operational effectiveness.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eImproving detection, response, and resilience capabilities across the enterprise environment.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePartnering with infrastructure, workplace, cloud, networking, and engineering teams to embed security by design.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDriving the implementation of Zero Trust principles, including strong identity controls, least privilege, continuous verification, and network segmentation.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSupporting the secure adoption of AI technologies and helping establish technical guardrails that reduce risk while enabling innovation.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eImproving data protection and information security capabilities to ensure sensitive information is protected throughout its lifecycle.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eContributing to security architecture decisions and helping define future security capabilities and standards.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEvaluating new technologies and continuously improving security tooling, integrations, and processes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eServing as a Tier 3 security engineering escalation point for complex incidents and high-priority security events.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eParticipating in a shared on-call rotation supporting our Security Operations Centre (SOC) for approximately five weeks annually.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch4\u003eWho you are\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou are a hands-on cybersecurity engineer who enjoys solving technical security challenges and building scalable security solutions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou combine strong security engineering expertise with a pragmatic mindset and understand how to balance security, usability, and business objectives. You are comfortable working across engineering, operations, and automation, and can translate security requirements into effective technical controls.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eMost importantly, you view security tooling and processes as systems that can be engineered, automated, and continuously improved.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou bring:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAt least 5 years of hands-on experience in cybersecurity engineering.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong technical understanding of enterprise security architectures and controls.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience implementing security solutions across endpoint, identity, network, and data protection domains.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience building automations, integrations, or custom tooling to improve security operations and engineering outcomes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong scripting and problem-solving skills.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience working in cloud-first and modern enterprise environments.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAbility to collaborate effectively with both technical and non-technical stakeholders.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eA passion for continuous improvement and a builder’s mindset.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou have experience with:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMicrosoft security technologies.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eData protection, data security, privacy, and DLP.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEndpoint security and device management.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eNetwork security and Zero Trust architectures.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEmail and collaboration security.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSecurity automation, orchestration, and scripting.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eInfrastructure-as-Code (IaC) and secure configuration management.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn addition, you may also have experience with:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIdentity, access, and privilege management.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePublic Key Infrastructure (PKI) and cryptographic controls.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAI security, governance, and risk management.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou are motivated by creating meaningful impact and helping strengthen security capabilities across identities, endpoints, networks, and data. You enjoy increasing automation, improving resilience, expanding Zero Trust adoption, and enabling the secure and responsible use of emerging technologies, including AI.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate-neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative. Together, we are creating, collaborating, and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility. We are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eIs this you?\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf you are interested in joining the Polestar crew, don’t wait to submit your application. As part of our recruitment process, you may be asked to complete assessments and participate in background checks relevant to the position. We apply a continuous selection process, and the job posting will remain open until the position is filled. \u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric, by the way…\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Cybersecurity Engineer","description":"\u003ch4\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is accelerating the transition to sustainable mobility through electric performance. As a digital-first, cloud-driven organisation, cybersecurity is a critical enabler of our business, products, and services.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are looking for a Cybersecurity Engineer to strengthen and evolve our enterprise security capabilities. This role focuses on designing, implementing, operating, and continuously improving security controls that protect our workforce, data, identities, devices, networks, and digital services.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis is not a traditional operations-focused security role. We are looking for an engineer who enjoys building, automating, and improving security capabilities at scale while working closely with technology teams across the organisation.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs a Cybersecurity Engineer, you will play a key role in strengthening Polestar’s enterprise security posture and advancing our Zero Trust journey. You will help build scalable security capabilities that protect users, devices, identities, data, and enterprise services in a modern cloud-first environment.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis role is located at: \u003cstrong\u003ePolestar Headquarters, Gothenburg, Sweden.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe believe in empowerment and support flexible working hours and a hybrid way of working.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eWhat you’ll do\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will work across security engineering, automation, and operational resilience, partnering with teams throughout the organisation to embed security by design and continuously improve enterprise security capabilities.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis includes:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eImplementing and continuously improving security capabilities across endpoint, identity, network, collaboration, and data protection domains.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSupporting the deployment, optimisation, and governance of enterprise security platforms and controls.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eBuilding and maintaining security automations that reduce manual effort and improve operational effectiveness.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eImproving detection, response, and resilience capabilities across the enterprise environment.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePartnering with infrastructure, workplace, cloud, networking, and engineering teams to embed security by design.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDriving the implementation of Zero Trust principles, including strong identity controls, least privilege, continuous verification, and network segmentation.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSupporting the secure adoption of AI technologies and helping establish technical guardrails that reduce risk while enabling innovation.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eImproving data protection and information security capabilities to ensure sensitive information is protected throughout its lifecycle.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eContributing to security architecture decisions and helping define future security capabilities and standards.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEvaluating new technologies and continuously improving security tooling, integrations, and processes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eServing as a Tier 3 security engineering escalation point for complex incidents and high-priority security events.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eParticipating in a shared on-call rotation supporting our Security Operations Centre (SOC) for approximately five weeks annually.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch4\u003eWho you are\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou are a hands-on cybersecurity engineer who enjoys solving technical security challenges and building scalable security solutions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou combine strong security engineering expertise with a pragmatic mindset and understand how to balance security, usability, and business objectives. You are comfortable working across engineering, operations, and automation, and can translate security requirements into effective technical controls.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eMost importantly, you view security tooling and processes as systems that can be engineered, automated, and continuously improved.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou bring:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAt least 5 years of hands-on experience in cybersecurity engineering.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong technical understanding of enterprise security architectures and controls.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience implementing security solutions across endpoint, identity, network, and data protection domains.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience building automations, integrations, or custom tooling to improve security operations and engineering outcomes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong scripting and problem-solving skills.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience working in cloud-first and modern enterprise environments.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAbility to collaborate effectively with both technical and non-technical stakeholders.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eA passion for continuous improvement and a builder’s mindset.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou have experience with:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMicrosoft security technologies.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eData protection, data security, privacy, and DLP.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEndpoint security and device management.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eNetwork security and Zero Trust architectures.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEmail and collaboration security.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSecurity automation, orchestration, and scripting.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eInfrastructure-as-Code (IaC) and secure configuration management.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn addition, you may also have experience with:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIdentity, access, and privilege management.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePublic Key Infrastructure (PKI) and cryptographic controls.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAI security, governance, and risk management.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou are motivated by creating meaningful impact and helping strengthen security capabilities across identities, endpoints, networks, and data. You enjoy increasing automation, improving resilience, expanding Zero Trust adoption, and enabling the secure and responsible use of emerging technologies, including AI.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate-neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative. Together, we are creating, collaborating, and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility. We are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eIs this you?\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf you are interested in joining the Polestar crew, don’t wait to submit your application. As part of our recruitment process, you may be asked to complete assessments and participate in background checks relevant to the position. We apply a continuous selection process, and the job posting will remain open until the position is filled. \u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric, by the way…\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":8260328},"datePosted":"2026-08-24T00:00:00+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Assar Gabrielssons väg 9","addressLocality":"Göteborg","postalCode":"418 78","addressCountry":"SE","addressRegion":"Nordics \u0026 UK"}}]}},{"id":"37a8ca66-7cf2-4657-8906-1fca88dccb5a","title":"Corporate Legal Counsel","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/8255359-corporate-legal-counsel","date_published":"2026-08-21T17:30:08+02:00","content_html":"\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWe're currently looking for a Corporate Legal Counsel to join our Corporate Legal team. In this role, you will provide strategic legal advice and support across a broad range of corporate, governance, securities regulation, capital markets, finance, and transaction-related matters. You will play a key role in supporting Polestar's listed parent company and global corporate structure, helping ensure compliance with regulatory requirements while enabling the business to achieve its strategic objectives.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAs part of the Legal function, you will work closely with executive management, the Board of Directors, and stakeholders across Finance, Treasury, Accounting, Sustainability, Investor Relations, and Corporate Communications. You will advise on governance matters, corporate transactions, capital markets activities, public company compliance, and other strategic initiatives that support Polestar's continued growth and transformation.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThis position is located in HQ, Gothenburg, Sweden. We believe in a hybrid model when it comes to remote and onsite work, knowing that both in-person collaboration and individual focus time are important for success.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe responsibilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn this role, you'll be a trusted business partner, providing practical legal advice to support strategic and operational decision-making across Polestar, while helping to maintain strong corporate governance and regulatory compliance.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eKey responsibilities include:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLead and support legal work relating to capital markets transactions, including debt and equity financings and other strategic corporate finance initiatives.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAdvise on corporate governance matters relating to Polestar's listed parent company and global subsidiaries.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSupport compliance with securities regulations, SEC requirements, and NASDAQ listing rules.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAdvise on corporate policies, procedures, governance best practices, and compliance with market abuse and insider trading regulations.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eManage and coordinate external legal counsel across multiple jurisdictions, ensuring effective delivery and budget oversight.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePartner with senior stakeholders across the business to provide pragmatic legal advice that balances risk management with commercial objective.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe ideal candidate\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eTo succeed in this role, you'll need excellent legal judgment, strong business acumen, and the ability to navigate complex legal matters in a fast-paced international environment. You combine technical legal expertise with a practical, solution-oriented mindset and are comfortable working independently while collaborating effectively with senior stakeholders across the organization. You thrive in a dynamic environment where priorities evolve, and you enjoy working on a diverse range of high-impact corporate and strategic matters.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn addition, you'll need the following qualifications:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMaster degree in Law (LLM), preferably from relevant Swedish, U.S., or other European university.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExtensive relevant experience (approximately 7+ years), including experience from a leading law firm and in-house legal roles within a global publicly listed company.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong experience in securities regulation, disclosure requirements, capital markets transactions, corporate finance, M\u0026amp;A, and general corporate matters.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eKnowledge of Swedish, U.K. and/or U.S. corporate law.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eProven experience advising on public company compliance, corporate governance, and stock exchange regulations.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience of supporting a Board and/or Committee, preparing Board and Committee materials, including advising on governance processes and regulatory requirements.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience managing external legal counsel and coordinating support across multiple jurisdictions.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExcellent written and verbal communication skills in English.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eBeneficial, but not required:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience with SEC, NASDAQ and Sarbanes-Oxley rules and compliance.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFamiliarity with Loan Market Association documentation.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience managing complex litigation matters, particularly in the U.S.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFamiliarity with IFRS accounting and audit practices.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFamiliarity with U.S. and European audit practices\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience with equity incentive plans.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAdditional European languages and/or Mandarin proficiency\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePolestar is an international company with colleagues representing diverse backgrounds and perspectives. English is our primary language for written and spoken communication. As we continue to grow globally, change is constant, but so is progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment where your expertise will have visible impact across the organization.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIf the above matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. We apply a continuous selection process and the job ad will be open until the position is filled.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Corporate Legal Counsel","description":"\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWe're currently looking for a Corporate Legal Counsel to join our Corporate Legal team. In this role, you will provide strategic legal advice and support across a broad range of corporate, governance, securities regulation, capital markets, finance, and transaction-related matters. You will play a key role in supporting Polestar's listed parent company and global corporate structure, helping ensure compliance with regulatory requirements while enabling the business to achieve its strategic objectives.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAs part of the Legal function, you will work closely with executive management, the Board of Directors, and stakeholders across Finance, Treasury, Accounting, Sustainability, Investor Relations, and Corporate Communications. You will advise on governance matters, corporate transactions, capital markets activities, public company compliance, and other strategic initiatives that support Polestar's continued growth and transformation.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThis position is located in HQ, Gothenburg, Sweden. We believe in a hybrid model when it comes to remote and onsite work, knowing that both in-person collaboration and individual focus time are important for success.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe responsibilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn this role, you'll be a trusted business partner, providing practical legal advice to support strategic and operational decision-making across Polestar, while helping to maintain strong corporate governance and regulatory compliance.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eKey responsibilities include:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLead and support legal work relating to capital markets transactions, including debt and equity financings and other strategic corporate finance initiatives.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAdvise on corporate governance matters relating to Polestar's listed parent company and global subsidiaries.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSupport compliance with securities regulations, SEC requirements, and NASDAQ listing rules.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAdvise on corporate policies, procedures, governance best practices, and compliance with market abuse and insider trading regulations.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eManage and coordinate external legal counsel across multiple jurisdictions, ensuring effective delivery and budget oversight.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePartner with senior stakeholders across the business to provide pragmatic legal advice that balances risk management with commercial objective.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe ideal candidate\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eTo succeed in this role, you'll need excellent legal judgment, strong business acumen, and the ability to navigate complex legal matters in a fast-paced international environment. You combine technical legal expertise with a practical, solution-oriented mindset and are comfortable working independently while collaborating effectively with senior stakeholders across the organization. You thrive in a dynamic environment where priorities evolve, and you enjoy working on a diverse range of high-impact corporate and strategic matters.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn addition, you'll need the following qualifications:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMaster degree in Law (LLM), preferably from relevant Swedish, U.S., or other European university.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExtensive relevant experience (approximately 7+ years), including experience from a leading law firm and in-house legal roles within a global publicly listed company.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong experience in securities regulation, disclosure requirements, capital markets transactions, corporate finance, M\u0026amp;A, and general corporate matters.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eKnowledge of Swedish, U.K. and/or U.S. corporate law.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eProven experience advising on public company compliance, corporate governance, and stock exchange regulations.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience of supporting a Board and/or Committee, preparing Board and Committee materials, including advising on governance processes and regulatory requirements.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience managing external legal counsel and coordinating support across multiple jurisdictions.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExcellent written and verbal communication skills in English.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eBeneficial, but not required:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience with SEC, NASDAQ and Sarbanes-Oxley rules and compliance.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFamiliarity with Loan Market Association documentation.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience managing complex litigation matters, particularly in the U.S.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFamiliarity with IFRS accounting and audit practices.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFamiliarity with U.S. and European audit practices\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience with equity incentive plans.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAdditional European languages and/or Mandarin proficiency\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePolestar is an international company with colleagues representing diverse backgrounds and perspectives. English is our primary language for written and spoken communication. As we continue to grow globally, change is constant, but so is progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment where your expertise will have visible impact across the organization.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIf the above matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. We apply a continuous selection process and the job ad will be open until the position is filled.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":8255359},"datePosted":"2026-08-21T17:30:08+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Assar Gabrielssons väg 9","addressLocality":"Göteborg","postalCode":"418 78","addressCountry":"SE","addressRegion":"Nordics \u0026 UK"}}]}},{"id":"c6cd510a-af2d-4890-9c20-8b8a73084feb","title":"Group Control Assurance Specialist","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/8253125-group-control-assurance-specialist","date_published":"2026-08-21T12:17:32+02:00","content_html":"\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eGroup Control Assurance Specialist is part of Finance department, Group Accounting, and the Group Control Assurance function and partners closely with stakeholders across the organization to resolve complex control, governance, and risk-related challenges.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eYou will be responsible to facilitate the evolution and effectiveness of the SOX internal control framework by leading control design initiatives, challenging existing processes, evaluating significant control deficiencies, and facilitating sustainable remediation solutions. Working in a fast-paced international environment, you will leverage your expertise to influence stakeholders, guide decision-making, and improve control maturity across business functions while ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe position is located at our HQ in Gothenburg, Sweden. We believe in empowerment and support flexible working hours and the possibility to work from home a couple of days per week.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat you'll do\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eYou will lead the continuous enhancement of Polestar's SOX internal control environment by applying advanced professional judgment to complex control matters, driving organizational improvements, and partnering with stakeholders across the business to strengthen risk management and governance practices.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eYou will:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLead the development and continuous enhancement of risk and control matrices, process documentation, and control frameworks by identifying underlying risks, challenging existing control environments, and driving the implementation of effective and sustainable control solutions.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDesign and drive the implementation of new controls and control improvement initiatives, partnering with process and control owners to establish practical solutions that address business risks while supporting operational objectives.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFacilitate the management testing program by defining testing strategies, ensuring high-quality execution, and driving timely completion across the organization.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eEvaluate control deficiencies, perform severity assessments, and provide expert analysis on business, financial reporting, and compliance impacts while facilitating stakeholder alignment on remediation priorities.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFacilitate the remediation of control deficiencies, significant deficiencies, and material weaknesses by influencing stakeholders, challenging root causes, and monitoring the implementation of sustainable corrective actions.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eServe as a trusted advisor to the organization by delivering specialized training, workshops, and guidance on internal controls, risk mitigation, governance practices, and remediation activities, including matters related to material weaknesses.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIdentify and lead cross-functional improvement initiatives that enhance the efficiency, effectiveness, and maturity of internal control, governance, and assurance processes across the organization.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eBuild strong relationships and collaborate with senior stakeholders, auditors, consultants, and business leaders to resolve complex issues and support the ongoing development of Polestar's control environment.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWho you are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eYou are a highly analytical and proactive professional with substantial experience in internal control, risk management, and assurance within complex and regulated environments. You are comfortable navigating ambiguity, solving complex challenges, communicating with stakeholders at all organizational levels, and contributing to a growing, fast‑paced organization.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eYou combine technical expertise with strong business acumen and are capable of independently assessing complex situations, developing practical solutions, and facilitating organizational change.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eTo be a great fit for this position, we believe you have:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e5+ years of experience in internal control, SOX, SEC reporting requirements within a U.S. - listed company environment, risk advisory, assurance, or related areas, ideally gained through a combination of industry and/or Big Four experience.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience working in multinational organizations.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDeep knowledge of risk assessment, process and system scoping, control design, implementation, testing, and control remediation.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience evaluating control deficiencies, including significant deficiencies and material weaknesses, and presenting conclusions to management.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eGeneral knowledge of group consolidation and IFRS reporting requirements.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eRelevant certifications such as CA, CPA, ACCA, CIA, or equivalent are considered an advantage.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePolestar is an international company with colleagues representing diverse backgrounds and perspectives. English is our primary language for written and spoken communication. As we continue to grow globally, change is constant, but so is progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment where your work will have visible impact.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIf the above matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. We apply a continuous selection process and the job ad will be open until the position is filled.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Group Control Assurance Specialist","description":"\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eGroup Control Assurance Specialist is part of Finance department, Group Accounting, and the Group Control Assurance function and partners closely with stakeholders across the organization to resolve complex control, governance, and risk-related challenges.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eYou will be responsible to facilitate the evolution and effectiveness of the SOX internal control framework by leading control design initiatives, challenging existing processes, evaluating significant control deficiencies, and facilitating sustainable remediation solutions. Working in a fast-paced international environment, you will leverage your expertise to influence stakeholders, guide decision-making, and improve control maturity across business functions while ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe position is located at our HQ in Gothenburg, Sweden. We believe in empowerment and support flexible working hours and the possibility to work from home a couple of days per week.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat you'll do\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eYou will lead the continuous enhancement of Polestar's SOX internal control environment by applying advanced professional judgment to complex control matters, driving organizational improvements, and partnering with stakeholders across the business to strengthen risk management and governance practices.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eYou will:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLead the development and continuous enhancement of risk and control matrices, process documentation, and control frameworks by identifying underlying risks, challenging existing control environments, and driving the implementation of effective and sustainable control solutions.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDesign and drive the implementation of new controls and control improvement initiatives, partnering with process and control owners to establish practical solutions that address business risks while supporting operational objectives.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFacilitate the management testing program by defining testing strategies, ensuring high-quality execution, and driving timely completion across the organization.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eEvaluate control deficiencies, perform severity assessments, and provide expert analysis on business, financial reporting, and compliance impacts while facilitating stakeholder alignment on remediation priorities.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFacilitate the remediation of control deficiencies, significant deficiencies, and material weaknesses by influencing stakeholders, challenging root causes, and monitoring the implementation of sustainable corrective actions.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eServe as a trusted advisor to the organization by delivering specialized training, workshops, and guidance on internal controls, risk mitigation, governance practices, and remediation activities, including matters related to material weaknesses.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIdentify and lead cross-functional improvement initiatives that enhance the efficiency, effectiveness, and maturity of internal control, governance, and assurance processes across the organization.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eBuild strong relationships and collaborate with senior stakeholders, auditors, consultants, and business leaders to resolve complex issues and support the ongoing development of Polestar's control environment.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWho you are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eYou are a highly analytical and proactive professional with substantial experience in internal control, risk management, and assurance within complex and regulated environments. You are comfortable navigating ambiguity, solving complex challenges, communicating with stakeholders at all organizational levels, and contributing to a growing, fast‑paced organization.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eYou combine technical expertise with strong business acumen and are capable of independently assessing complex situations, developing practical solutions, and facilitating organizational change.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eTo be a great fit for this position, we believe you have:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e5+ years of experience in internal control, SOX, SEC reporting requirements within a U.S. - listed company environment, risk advisory, assurance, or related areas, ideally gained through a combination of industry and/or Big Four experience.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience working in multinational organizations.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDeep knowledge of risk assessment, process and system scoping, control design, implementation, testing, and control remediation.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience evaluating control deficiencies, including significant deficiencies and material weaknesses, and presenting conclusions to management.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eGeneral knowledge of group consolidation and IFRS reporting requirements.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eRelevant certifications such as CA, CPA, ACCA, CIA, or equivalent are considered an advantage.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePolestar is an international company with colleagues representing diverse backgrounds and perspectives. English is our primary language for written and spoken communication. As we continue to grow globally, change is constant, but so is progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment where your work will have visible impact.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIf the above matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. We apply a continuous selection process and the job ad will be open until the position is filled.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":8253125},"datePosted":"2026-08-21T12:17:32+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Assar Gabrielssons väg 9","addressLocality":"Göteborg","postalCode":"418 78","addressCountry":"SE","addressRegion":"Nordics \u0026 UK"}}]}},{"id":"f0de524f-8899-483f-878b-7925b7703c49","title":"Senior Software Engineer – Car Services and Industrial Operations","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/7571552-senior-software-engineer-car-services-and-industrial-operations","date_published":"2026-08-17T00:00:00+02:00","content_html":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is accelerating the transition to sustainable mobility through electric performance. \u003cstrong\u003eCar Services and Industrial Operations\u003c/strong\u003e is a newly established area that plays a vital role in Polestar’s business. Our mission is to ensure that Polestar can offer services to customers seamlessly, while giving our service partners the digital tools they need to enhance, maintain, and repair our vehicles.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe support compound operations to ensure cars are properly prepared and delivered to their owners on time. We also collect, analyze, and share data that provides valuable product insights, helping the Quality organization to quickly identify and resolve issues, keeping customers satisfied and reducing quality costs. Product compliance is another cornerstone of our work, ensuring that Polestar’s products meet both new and existing legislation across all markets.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn addition, we support contract manufacturing by enabling downstream processes such as homologation, Certification of Conformity, and warranty handling. Sustainability is at the heart of what we do. Through smart digital solutions, we contribute to Polestar’s vision of a more sustainable future by making key data accessible across manufacturing, logistics, aftermarket, and sustainability, empowering better decisions, streamlined operations, and an elevated customer experience.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are now looking for a \u003cstrong\u003eSenior Software Engineer – Car Services and Industrial Operations\u003c/strong\u003e to join us at our headquarters in Gothenburg.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will join a close‑knit and experienced team, where several of us have worked together for a long time. This has shaped a cohesive group that collaborates seamlessly and supports one another. We are driven by ambition and set high standards for ourselves, while remaining prestige‑free and customer‑focused.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs a Senior Software Engineer, you will transform the Car Services and Industrial Operations area’s digital vision into working solutions by building and maintaining digital products, platforms, and services. You will work in close collaboration with Designers, Product Owners, Tech Leads, and Business Analysts to balance technical functionality, end‑user experience, and business value.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will have a direct influence on how our digital solutions function and how users interact with them. You will also stay on top of the evolving technology landscape and continuously invest in developing your skills.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will report to the Head of Car Services and Industrial Operations. This position is located at our HQ in Gothenburg, Sweden. We believe in empowerment and offer flexible working hours and the possibility to work from home a couple of days per week.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat you'll do\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will design, build, and maintain digital solutions that enable Car Services and Industrial Operations to deliver value across Polestar’s ecosystem.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eYou will:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDesign and develop software for digital products and services\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEnsure code follows Polestar’s coding practices and industry standards\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eWrite unit and integration tests, and develop automated tests where applicable\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eChallenge ideas and opinions to avoid pitfalls and inefficient solutions\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMaintain close collaboration with Architecture \u0026amp; Analytics to ensure that the latest guidelines and guardrails are followed when developing digital products, platforms, and services\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWho you are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou are a patient, resilient, and open individual who excels at communicating and explaining complex technical concepts. You value trust, transparency, and innovation, and you constantly look for ways to improve both solutions and ways of working.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou balance quality with pragmatism, align stakeholders on technical decisions, and connect people to enable efficient collaboration. You are passionate about technology and excited about the impact of emerging technologies, and you are open to learning new ideas beyond your current scope or skill set.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTo be a great fit for this position, we believe you have:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong knowledge of programming and engineering principles\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience building global, high‑performance, and scalable solutions\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAbility to write effective unit, integration, and other automated tests\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eKnowledge of DevOps practices and CI/CD pipelines\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience working as a developer in a cross‑functional agile team is preferred\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong problem‑solving skills with the ability to quickly process and analyze information\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience in system design using the following technology stack:\u003cbr\u003eNode.js / TypeScript, AWS Lambda, AWS Step Functions, Amazon EventBridge, DynamoDB, React / Remix, \u003cspan\u003eAthena SQL\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience using version control systems such as GitHub\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMore than 8 years of relevant professional experience\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that a change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate‑neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative. Together, we are creating, collaborating, and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility. We are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs this you?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf you are interested in joining the Polestar crew, don’t wait to submit your application. We apply a continuous selection process and the job post will remain open until the position is filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric, by the way…\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Senior Software Engineer – Car Services and Industrial Operations","description":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is accelerating the transition to sustainable mobility through electric performance. \u003cstrong\u003eCar Services and Industrial Operations\u003c/strong\u003e is a newly established area that plays a vital role in Polestar’s business. Our mission is to ensure that Polestar can offer services to customers seamlessly, while giving our service partners the digital tools they need to enhance, maintain, and repair our vehicles.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe support compound operations to ensure cars are properly prepared and delivered to their owners on time. We also collect, analyze, and share data that provides valuable product insights, helping the Quality organization to quickly identify and resolve issues, keeping customers satisfied and reducing quality costs. Product compliance is another cornerstone of our work, ensuring that Polestar’s products meet both new and existing legislation across all markets.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn addition, we support contract manufacturing by enabling downstream processes such as homologation, Certification of Conformity, and warranty handling. Sustainability is at the heart of what we do. Through smart digital solutions, we contribute to Polestar’s vision of a more sustainable future by making key data accessible across manufacturing, logistics, aftermarket, and sustainability, empowering better decisions, streamlined operations, and an elevated customer experience.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are now looking for a \u003cstrong\u003eSenior Software Engineer – Car Services and Industrial Operations\u003c/strong\u003e to join us at our headquarters in Gothenburg.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will join a close‑knit and experienced team, where several of us have worked together for a long time. This has shaped a cohesive group that collaborates seamlessly and supports one another. We are driven by ambition and set high standards for ourselves, while remaining prestige‑free and customer‑focused.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs a Senior Software Engineer, you will transform the Car Services and Industrial Operations area’s digital vision into working solutions by building and maintaining digital products, platforms, and services. You will work in close collaboration with Designers, Product Owners, Tech Leads, and Business Analysts to balance technical functionality, end‑user experience, and business value.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will have a direct influence on how our digital solutions function and how users interact with them. You will also stay on top of the evolving technology landscape and continuously invest in developing your skills.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will report to the Head of Car Services and Industrial Operations. This position is located at our HQ in Gothenburg, Sweden. We believe in empowerment and offer flexible working hours and the possibility to work from home a couple of days per week.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat you'll do\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will design, build, and maintain digital solutions that enable Car Services and Industrial Operations to deliver value across Polestar’s ecosystem.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eYou will:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDesign and develop software for digital products and services\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEnsure code follows Polestar’s coding practices and industry standards\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eWrite unit and integration tests, and develop automated tests where applicable\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eChallenge ideas and opinions to avoid pitfalls and inefficient solutions\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMaintain close collaboration with Architecture \u0026amp; Analytics to ensure that the latest guidelines and guardrails are followed when developing digital products, platforms, and services\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWho you are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou are a patient, resilient, and open individual who excels at communicating and explaining complex technical concepts. You value trust, transparency, and innovation, and you constantly look for ways to improve both solutions and ways of working.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou balance quality with pragmatism, align stakeholders on technical decisions, and connect people to enable efficient collaboration. You are passionate about technology and excited about the impact of emerging technologies, and you are open to learning new ideas beyond your current scope or skill set.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTo be a great fit for this position, we believe you have:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong knowledge of programming and engineering principles\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience building global, high‑performance, and scalable solutions\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAbility to write effective unit, integration, and other automated tests\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eKnowledge of DevOps practices and CI/CD pipelines\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience working as a developer in a cross‑functional agile team is preferred\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong problem‑solving skills with the ability to quickly process and analyze information\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience in system design using the following technology stack:\u003cbr\u003eNode.js / TypeScript, AWS Lambda, AWS Step Functions, Amazon EventBridge, DynamoDB, React / Remix, \u003cspan\u003eAthena SQL\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience using version control systems such as GitHub\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMore than 8 years of relevant professional experience\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that a change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate‑neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative. Together, we are creating, collaborating, and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility. We are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs this you?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf you are interested in joining the Polestar crew, don’t wait to submit your application. We apply a continuous selection process and the job post will remain open until the position is filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric, by the way…\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":7571552},"datePosted":"2026-08-17T00:00:00+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Assar Gabrielssons väg 9","addressLocality":"Göteborg","postalCode":"418 78","addressCountry":"SE","addressRegion":"Nordics \u0026 UK"}}]}},{"id":"d14ee7f6-e17e-4ef9-9a0f-228be7e5717a","title":"Group Accountant to Gothenburg HQ","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/7531097-group-accountant-to-gothenburg-hq","date_published":"2026-08-11T00:00:00+02:00","content_html":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is accelerating the transition to sustainable mobility through electric performance. As we continue to grow as a U.S.-listed, global organization, we are strengthening our Group Finance function and are now looking for a \u003cstrong\u003eGroup Accountant\u003c/strong\u003e to join our Group Accounting team at our headquarters in Gothenburg.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn this role, you will be part of the Group Accounting team, playing a key role in ensuring high-quality, timely, and accurate consolidated financial reporting for the Polestar Group. The position has a strong focus on group closings, consolidation, and external financial reporting, including IFRS reporting and SEC filings with Nasdaq in New York.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will work closely with subsidiaries, internal stakeholders, and external auditors, contributing to a consistent and compliant financial reporting framework across the Group. This is an excellent opportunity for someone who enjoys working in a global, scale-up environment where processes continue to evolve and improve.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis position is located at our HQ, in Gothenburg. We understand that work-life balance isn’t easy, and of course, welcome our employees to work flexible hours and from home a couple of days per week if needed. We believe in empowerment.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat you'll do\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs a Group Accountant at Polestar, you will support the full cycle of group financial reporting and play an important role in delivering reliable financial information to both internal and external stakeholders. You will work hands-on with consolidation, analysis, and reporting and contribute to continuously improving our group accounting processes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will also collaborate closely with subsidiaries and finance teams across the organization to ensure accuracy, compliance, and consistency in financial reporting.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eYou will:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSupport monthly, quarterly, and annual group closing processes, including preparation and validation of consolidation and adjustment entries\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eCollaborate with subsidiaries and internal stakeholders to ensure timely and accurate financial submissions\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePerform financial analysis and prepare supporting documentation for internal and external reporting\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAssist in the preparation of external IFRS financial reports, including notes and disclosures for quarterly and annual filings\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMaintain and monitor consolidation system data to ensure consistency and data quality across group entities\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eContribute to the development, maintenance, and documentation of group accounting policies and processes\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eParticipate in group accounting projects, reporting improvements, and system enhancements\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eCoordinate with external auditors and support the audit process by providing documentation and explanations\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eProactively identify opportunities to improve group accounting procedures, controls, and reporting efficiency\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWho you are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou are a structured and analytical finance professional with a solid understanding of group accounting and financial reporting. You enjoy working in a dynamic, international environment and thrive when collaborating with different stakeholders. You combine attention to detail with a pragmatic mindset and are comfortable handling deadlines in a listed-company context.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou are proactive, communicative, and continuously look for ways to improve processes and ways of working.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTo be a great fit for this position we believe you have:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eA university degree in Business Administration, Finance, Accounting, or equivalent\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e5–7 years of relevant experience within group accounting, a global corporate finance function, or an audit firm\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSolid knowledge of IFRS accounting standards and group consolidation principles\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience working with monthly, quarterly, and annual closing processes\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong Excel skills and confidence working with financial analysis and reporting\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience with consolidation systems; \u003cstrong\u003eAARO experience is a strong advantage\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExposure to SOX compliance and reporting for U.S.-listed companies is considered a plus\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eFluency in English, both written and spoken\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eAt Polestar, you will be part of a cross-functional and international team, with English as a natural language for written and spoken communication. Since Polestar moves fast you thrive by working in a fast-paced environment.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that a change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate-neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative. Together, we are creating, collaborating, and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility. We are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs this you?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIf you are interested in joining the Polestar crew, don’t wait with submitting your application. We apply a continuous selection process and the job ad will be open until the position is filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric, by the way…\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Group Accountant to Gothenburg HQ","description":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is accelerating the transition to sustainable mobility through electric performance. As we continue to grow as a U.S.-listed, global organization, we are strengthening our Group Finance function and are now looking for a \u003cstrong\u003eGroup Accountant\u003c/strong\u003e to join our Group Accounting team at our headquarters in Gothenburg.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn this role, you will be part of the Group Accounting team, playing a key role in ensuring high-quality, timely, and accurate consolidated financial reporting for the Polestar Group. The position has a strong focus on group closings, consolidation, and external financial reporting, including IFRS reporting and SEC filings with Nasdaq in New York.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will work closely with subsidiaries, internal stakeholders, and external auditors, contributing to a consistent and compliant financial reporting framework across the Group. This is an excellent opportunity for someone who enjoys working in a global, scale-up environment where processes continue to evolve and improve.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis position is located at our HQ, in Gothenburg. We understand that work-life balance isn’t easy, and of course, welcome our employees to work flexible hours and from home a couple of days per week if needed. We believe in empowerment.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat you'll do\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs a Group Accountant at Polestar, you will support the full cycle of group financial reporting and play an important role in delivering reliable financial information to both internal and external stakeholders. You will work hands-on with consolidation, analysis, and reporting and contribute to continuously improving our group accounting processes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will also collaborate closely with subsidiaries and finance teams across the organization to ensure accuracy, compliance, and consistency in financial reporting.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eYou will:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSupport monthly, quarterly, and annual group closing processes, including preparation and validation of consolidation and adjustment entries\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eCollaborate with subsidiaries and internal stakeholders to ensure timely and accurate financial submissions\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePerform financial analysis and prepare supporting documentation for internal and external reporting\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAssist in the preparation of external IFRS financial reports, including notes and disclosures for quarterly and annual filings\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMaintain and monitor consolidation system data to ensure consistency and data quality across group entities\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eContribute to the development, maintenance, and documentation of group accounting policies and processes\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eParticipate in group accounting projects, reporting improvements, and system enhancements\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eCoordinate with external auditors and support the audit process by providing documentation and explanations\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eProactively identify opportunities to improve group accounting procedures, controls, and reporting efficiency\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWho you are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou are a structured and analytical finance professional with a solid understanding of group accounting and financial reporting. You enjoy working in a dynamic, international environment and thrive when collaborating with different stakeholders. You combine attention to detail with a pragmatic mindset and are comfortable handling deadlines in a listed-company context.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou are proactive, communicative, and continuously look for ways to improve processes and ways of working.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTo be a great fit for this position we believe you have:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eA university degree in Business Administration, Finance, Accounting, or equivalent\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e5–7 years of relevant experience within group accounting, a global corporate finance function, or an audit firm\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSolid knowledge of IFRS accounting standards and group consolidation principles\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience working with monthly, quarterly, and annual closing processes\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong Excel skills and confidence working with financial analysis and reporting\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience with consolidation systems; \u003cstrong\u003eAARO experience is a strong advantage\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExposure to SOX compliance and reporting for U.S.-listed companies is considered a plus\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eFluency in English, both written and spoken\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eAt Polestar, you will be part of a cross-functional and international team, with English as a natural language for written and spoken communication. Since Polestar moves fast you thrive by working in a fast-paced environment.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that a change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate-neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative. Together, we are creating, collaborating, and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility. We are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs this you?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIf you are interested in joining the Polestar crew, don’t wait with submitting your application. We apply a continuous selection process and the job ad will be open until the position is filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric, by the way…\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":7531097},"datePosted":"2026-08-11T00:00:00+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Assar Gabrielssons väg 9","addressLocality":"Göteborg","postalCode":"418 78","addressCountry":"SE","addressRegion":"Nordics \u0026 UK"}}]}},{"id":"86ab9121-f6ec-4f59-b8ec-fa963e9c42dd","title":"Order Specialist (Young Graduate)","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/8119049-order-specialist-young-graduate","date_published":"2026-07-24T10:29:51+02:00","content_html":"\u003cp\u003eWe're currently looking for a Junior Operations Specialist with a focus on Order Processing to join our Operations team. Someone with a passion for electric mobility, an interest in technology, and a desire to create the change we know is needed.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis position is located at Polestar Belgium in Brussels and is limited to two years. We believe in a hybrid model when it comes to remote and onsite work, knowing that both in-person collaboration and individual time to focus are needed. What matters most is that people get the time, and support, to do what needs to be done. And to enjoy doing it, of course.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn this role, you'll be expected to support the Planning, Ordering and Distribution Manager Belgium. Your key responsibility will be to process incoming orders from new and existing fleet or B2B customers. You will be in close contact with the Sales Team in order to ensure orders are processed efficiently and effectively. You will also be in close contact with the leasing companies and our headquarters in Sweden to ensure timely and correct order processing. A second part of the job is to monitor, analyze, optimize and automate existing (order) processes within the Operations Team, to make our organization future proof.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat you'll do\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eProcess incoming fleet orders daily (review, validation, and approval), sharing responsibility with the Sales Department for order processing speed and First Time Right (FTR) percentage.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEstablish, monitor and analyze relevant internal reports\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eOrganize and stimulate internal cross-departmental alignment for order processing\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAssess and improve current ordering processes for fleet and business orders\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSupport the continuous training of internal and external stakeholders with regards to changes in the fleet ordering process\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eOptimize current business processes with the ambition to strive for Operational Excellence, focusing on improving the quality and processing speed of incoming orders by providing support in finding the root cause of errors, and by providing support in the implementation of processes that mitigate and address these errors\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePrepare and maintain order processing dashboards, providing regular feedback to internal stakeholders when needed\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSupport the Business Development Manager in implementing Sales Enablement processes affecting fleet order processing\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePrepare and update the order processing manual\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWho you are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn order to succeed in this role, and at Polestar in general, there are a few characteristics you'll need to have. Tenacity. Flexibility. Curiosity. We are looking for collaborative and communicative young graduate, with a high level of drive, used to taking initiatives and working independently. You are analytical and process driven with thorough attention to detail. The ability to take the initiative, to meet deadlines and requirements, and to abandon ideas when they're not feasible.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn addition, you'll need the following qualifications:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDegree in business administration, logistics or a related field, professional experience is not required.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eProblem-solving as well as organizational skills\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAbility to both work effectively in a team and independently\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExcellent level of spoken and written Dutch, French \u0026amp; English\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMS Excel/PowerPoint/Word\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is an international company, with various backgrounds represented. And though we have a global presence, we maintain the growth-mindset. Change happens often at Polestar. But so does progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that a change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate-neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative. Together, we are creating, collaborating and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs this you?\u003c/strong\u003e If you are interested in joining the Polestar crew, don't wait with submitting your application. We apply a continuous selection process and the job post will be open until the position is filled.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric by the way...\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Order Specialist (Young Graduate)","description":"\u003cp\u003eWe're currently looking for a Junior Operations Specialist with a focus on Order Processing to join our Operations team. Someone with a passion for electric mobility, an interest in technology, and a desire to create the change we know is needed.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis position is located at Polestar Belgium in Brussels and is limited to two years. We believe in a hybrid model when it comes to remote and onsite work, knowing that both in-person collaboration and individual time to focus are needed. What matters most is that people get the time, and support, to do what needs to be done. And to enjoy doing it, of course.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn this role, you'll be expected to support the Planning, Ordering and Distribution Manager Belgium. Your key responsibility will be to process incoming orders from new and existing fleet or B2B customers. You will be in close contact with the Sales Team in order to ensure orders are processed efficiently and effectively. You will also be in close contact with the leasing companies and our headquarters in Sweden to ensure timely and correct order processing. A second part of the job is to monitor, analyze, optimize and automate existing (order) processes within the Operations Team, to make our organization future proof.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat you'll do\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eProcess incoming fleet orders daily (review, validation, and approval), sharing responsibility with the Sales Department for order processing speed and First Time Right (FTR) percentage.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEstablish, monitor and analyze relevant internal reports\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eOrganize and stimulate internal cross-departmental alignment for order processing\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAssess and improve current ordering processes for fleet and business orders\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSupport the continuous training of internal and external stakeholders with regards to changes in the fleet ordering process\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eOptimize current business processes with the ambition to strive for Operational Excellence, focusing on improving the quality and processing speed of incoming orders by providing support in finding the root cause of errors, and by providing support in the implementation of processes that mitigate and address these errors\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePrepare and maintain order processing dashboards, providing regular feedback to internal stakeholders when needed\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSupport the Business Development Manager in implementing Sales Enablement processes affecting fleet order processing\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePrepare and update the order processing manual\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWho you are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn order to succeed in this role, and at Polestar in general, there are a few characteristics you'll need to have. Tenacity. Flexibility. Curiosity. We are looking for collaborative and communicative young graduate, with a high level of drive, used to taking initiatives and working independently. You are analytical and process driven with thorough attention to detail. The ability to take the initiative, to meet deadlines and requirements, and to abandon ideas when they're not feasible.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn addition, you'll need the following qualifications:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDegree in business administration, logistics or a related field, professional experience is not required.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eProblem-solving as well as organizational skills\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAbility to both work effectively in a team and independently\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExcellent level of spoken and written Dutch, French \u0026amp; English\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMS Excel/PowerPoint/Word\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is an international company, with various backgrounds represented. And though we have a global presence, we maintain the growth-mindset. Change happens often at Polestar. But so does progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that a change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate-neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative. Together, we are creating, collaborating and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs this you?\u003c/strong\u003e If you are interested in joining the Polestar crew, don't wait with submitting your application. We apply a continuous selection process and the job post will be open until the position is filled.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric by the way...\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":8119049},"datePosted":"2026-07-24T10:29:51+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":null,"addressLocality":"Brussels","postalCode":"1000","addressCountry":"BE","addressRegion":"EMEA"}}]}},{"id":"ced1f05b-ff8f-4f8c-b0cb-3441e3b4c7e6","title":"Group Category Manager – Digital","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/8052272-group-category-manager-digital","date_published":"2026-07-10T11:24:17+02:00","content_html":"\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWe're currently looking for a Group Category Manager – Digital. Someone to join our Procurement team in order to drive category strategies, optimize supplier performance, and create sustainable business value across Polestar's digital procurement landscape. Someone with a passion for business transformation, an interest in technology and digital services, and a desire to challenge the status quo to deliver measurable results.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAs a Group Category Manager for Digital, you'll lead a team responsible for specific categories of indirect goods and services. You will guide the team through strategic opportunity assessments, category planning, and competitive sourcing activities, while driving fact-based procurement initiatives through spend analysis, contract management, and supplier market exploration. You will play a crucial role in implementing category strategies that deliver sustainable value, enhance supplier performance, and support Polestar's long-term business objectives.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThis position is located in Polestar HQ, Gothenburg, Sweden. We believe in a hybrid model when it comes to remote and onsite work, knowing that both in-person collaboration and individual time to focus are needed.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe responsibilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn this role, you'll be expected to lead the Digital category and drive procurement performance with clear financial and operational impact. Working as a member of the Procurement organization, you'll be instrumental in developing category strategies, influencing stakeholders, and creating sustainable business value.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSee below for a more thorough breakdown of the various tasks and areas you'll be responsible for:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDevelop and execute category roadmaps and sourcing strategies that link procurement initiatives to financial outcomes, operational excellence, and business objectives.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDrive category performance through cost optimization, supplier performance management, value creation initiatives, and strategic negotiations with suppliers.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eBuild strong relationships with stakeholders across the business, challenge existing ways of working, and align internal and external partners around common goals.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLead, coach, and develop a team of procurement professionals while contributing to the ongoing transformation of Procurement into a strategic value business partner.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eProvide insights and recommendations to senior leadership, while building and maintaining strategic networks with suppliers, Geely Group, and Volvo Cars to drive synergies and business value.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe ideal candidate\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn order to succeed in this role, and at Polestar in general, there are a few characteristics you'll need to have. Tenacity. Flexibility. Curiosity. The ability to take initiative, influence stakeholders, and navigate complex business environments. You are a strategic thinker with strong leadership capabilities and the courage to challenge business needs and established ways of working when necessary. You thrive in change, communicate effectively at all levels, and are driven by delivering measurable business results through collaboration and data-driven decision-making.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn addition, you'll need the following qualifications:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eUniversity degree, preferably a Master's degree in Business Administration, Industrial Engineering \u0026amp; Management, or a related field, providing a strong foundation for strategic procurement and business decision-making.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e10+ years of relevant professional experience, including at least three years of people leadership experience, enabling you to successfully lead teams and drive organizational results.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExtensive experience in category management, procurement, strategic sourcing, and negotiations within a large enterprise environment. This expertise is essential for driving category performance and supplier value creation.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong analytical capabilities, including spend analysis, opportunity assessments, pricing model evaluation, and contract management, supporting fact-based decision-making and strategic planning.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExtensive experience within digital procurement categories, including digital hardware, software licensing, and digital services, combined with experience driving change and implementing strategies in complex organizations.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePolestar is an international company, with various backgrounds represented. English, therefore, is the language of written and spoken communication. And though we have a global presence, we maintain the growth-mindset. Change happens often at Polestar. But so does progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIf the above matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. Due to the summer holiday period, our recruitment process is moving at a slower pace, and we may not be able to provide updates in the meantime. We look forward to getting back to you during August.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Group Category Manager – Digital","description":"\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWe're currently looking for a Group Category Manager – Digital. Someone to join our Procurement team in order to drive category strategies, optimize supplier performance, and create sustainable business value across Polestar's digital procurement landscape. Someone with a passion for business transformation, an interest in technology and digital services, and a desire to challenge the status quo to deliver measurable results.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAs a Group Category Manager for Digital, you'll lead a team responsible for specific categories of indirect goods and services. You will guide the team through strategic opportunity assessments, category planning, and competitive sourcing activities, while driving fact-based procurement initiatives through spend analysis, contract management, and supplier market exploration. You will play a crucial role in implementing category strategies that deliver sustainable value, enhance supplier performance, and support Polestar's long-term business objectives.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThis position is located in Polestar HQ, Gothenburg, Sweden. We believe in a hybrid model when it comes to remote and onsite work, knowing that both in-person collaboration and individual time to focus are needed.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe responsibilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn this role, you'll be expected to lead the Digital category and drive procurement performance with clear financial and operational impact. Working as a member of the Procurement organization, you'll be instrumental in developing category strategies, influencing stakeholders, and creating sustainable business value.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSee below for a more thorough breakdown of the various tasks and areas you'll be responsible for:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDevelop and execute category roadmaps and sourcing strategies that link procurement initiatives to financial outcomes, operational excellence, and business objectives.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDrive category performance through cost optimization, supplier performance management, value creation initiatives, and strategic negotiations with suppliers.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eBuild strong relationships with stakeholders across the business, challenge existing ways of working, and align internal and external partners around common goals.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLead, coach, and develop a team of procurement professionals while contributing to the ongoing transformation of Procurement into a strategic value business partner.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eProvide insights and recommendations to senior leadership, while building and maintaining strategic networks with suppliers, Geely Group, and Volvo Cars to drive synergies and business value.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe ideal candidate\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn order to succeed in this role, and at Polestar in general, there are a few characteristics you'll need to have. Tenacity. Flexibility. Curiosity. The ability to take initiative, influence stakeholders, and navigate complex business environments. You are a strategic thinker with strong leadership capabilities and the courage to challenge business needs and established ways of working when necessary. You thrive in change, communicate effectively at all levels, and are driven by delivering measurable business results through collaboration and data-driven decision-making.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn addition, you'll need the following qualifications:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eUniversity degree, preferably a Master's degree in Business Administration, Industrial Engineering \u0026amp; Management, or a related field, providing a strong foundation for strategic procurement and business decision-making.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e10+ years of relevant professional experience, including at least three years of people leadership experience, enabling you to successfully lead teams and drive organizational results.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExtensive experience in category management, procurement, strategic sourcing, and negotiations within a large enterprise environment. This expertise is essential for driving category performance and supplier value creation.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong analytical capabilities, including spend analysis, opportunity assessments, pricing model evaluation, and contract management, supporting fact-based decision-making and strategic planning.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExtensive experience within digital procurement categories, including digital hardware, software licensing, and digital services, combined with experience driving change and implementing strategies in complex organizations.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePolestar is an international company, with various backgrounds represented. English, therefore, is the language of written and spoken communication. And though we have a global presence, we maintain the growth-mindset. Change happens often at Polestar. But so does progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIf the above matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. Due to the summer holiday period, our recruitment process is moving at a slower pace, and we may not be able to provide updates in the meantime. We look forward to getting back to you during August.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":8052272},"datePosted":"2026-07-10T11:24:17+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Assar Gabrielssons väg 9","addressLocality":"Göteborg","postalCode":"418 78","addressCountry":"SE","addressRegion":"Nordics \u0026 UK"}}]}},{"id":"ca22ecd9-aca2-4c1e-8e85-2ded753ba72a","title":"Aftersales Lead | Norway","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/8040532-aftersales-lead-norway","date_published":"2026-07-08T15:21:41+02:00","content_html":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eWe are currently looking for a Aftersales Lead which internally will be called Customer Service Lead. This person will be a key member of Polestar`s Customer Service Operations team where you will serve as a primary point\u003cspan\u003e \u003c/span\u003eof contact for workshops and external partners, where you will ensure smooth communication and collaboration, be responsible for coordinating service operations, addressing queries and providing support to workshops and partners to maintain a high service standard.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eA strong technical understanding of modern vehicles is a key requirement for this role. As Aftersales Lead, you will be responsible for driving product quality by identifying quality trends, analyzing field data, and leading investigations into vehicle-related issues. Working closely with engineering, service partners, and cross-functional teams, you will ensure that product concerns are escalated, root causes are identified, and corrective actions are implemented. Strong technical competence, analytical skills, and a passion for improving product quality are essential for success in this role.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eThis position is located at Polestar Norway HQ in Fornebu, Oslo. This role will mainly work onsite to really connect with your department and be able to better collaborate with the rest of our Polestar team. With this new position our Customer Service team will grow from one to two people where both will report directly to our Head of Customer Experience. Frequent business travel to our service and retail partners is an integral part of this role, and will be required on a regular basis.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe responsibilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eIn this role, you will be expected to drive aftersales performance, service quality and sustainable business growth across the network. As member of the Customer Service department in Norway you will be an important part of developing performance across the network as well as internally within the department.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eSee below for a more thorough breakdown of the various tasks and areas you will be responsible for:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\"\u003eDrive aftersales performance, service quality, and sustainable growth across Polestar’s service network.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSupport service partners in solving operational and technical challenges while maximizing customer retention and revenue.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAnalyze key aftersales KPIs and translate insights into actions that improve profitability and service performance.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eLead continuous improvement initiatives that optimize operations and enhance customer experience.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDeliver strategic service market projects and build strong partner relationships to grow revenue, loyalty, and network performance.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe ideal candidate\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eTo succeed in this role, and at Polestar In general, there are a few characteristics you will need to have. Curiosity. Flexibility. Tenacity. You will also need to have the ability to take initiative, build long-term relationships and have an eye for possible improvements and growth opportunities in a dynamic environment. You are driven by taking ownership, responsibility, optimalisation and collaboration. It is preferable that the candidate also has a strong analytical sense as well as having a strategic mindset to transform insights into initiatives.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eIn addition, you will need the following qualifications:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSolid experience within automotive aftersales, service network operations, or customer service management.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eRelevant degree in Business, Finance, Engineering, or equivalent professional experience.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience from the Polestar Service Network is considered a strong advantage.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDemonstrated ability to lead cross-functional projects and drive business and service improvements.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong data analysis capabilities with a track record of turning customer and operational insights into measurable results.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eIf you find the position interesting and the above description matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. Our selection process is ongoing, and the job advert will remain open until it’s filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Aftersales Lead | Norway","description":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eWe are currently looking for a Aftersales Lead which internally will be called Customer Service Lead. This person will be a key member of Polestar`s Customer Service Operations team where you will serve as a primary point\u003cspan\u003e \u003c/span\u003eof contact for workshops and external partners, where you will ensure smooth communication and collaboration, be responsible for coordinating service operations, addressing queries and providing support to workshops and partners to maintain a high service standard.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eA strong technical understanding of modern vehicles is a key requirement for this role. As Aftersales Lead, you will be responsible for driving product quality by identifying quality trends, analyzing field data, and leading investigations into vehicle-related issues. Working closely with engineering, service partners, and cross-functional teams, you will ensure that product concerns are escalated, root causes are identified, and corrective actions are implemented. Strong technical competence, analytical skills, and a passion for improving product quality are essential for success in this role.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eThis position is located at Polestar Norway HQ in Fornebu, Oslo. This role will mainly work onsite to really connect with your department and be able to better collaborate with the rest of our Polestar team. With this new position our Customer Service team will grow from one to two people where both will report directly to our Head of Customer Experience. Frequent business travel to our service and retail partners is an integral part of this role, and will be required on a regular basis.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe responsibilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eIn this role, you will be expected to drive aftersales performance, service quality and sustainable business growth across the network. As member of the Customer Service department in Norway you will be an important part of developing performance across the network as well as internally within the department.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eSee below for a more thorough breakdown of the various tasks and areas you will be responsible for:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\"\u003eDrive aftersales performance, service quality, and sustainable growth across Polestar’s service network.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSupport service partners in solving operational and technical challenges while maximizing customer retention and revenue.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAnalyze key aftersales KPIs and translate insights into actions that improve profitability and service performance.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eLead continuous improvement initiatives that optimize operations and enhance customer experience.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDeliver strategic service market projects and build strong partner relationships to grow revenue, loyalty, and network performance.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe ideal candidate\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eTo succeed in this role, and at Polestar In general, there are a few characteristics you will need to have. Curiosity. Flexibility. Tenacity. You will also need to have the ability to take initiative, build long-term relationships and have an eye for possible improvements and growth opportunities in a dynamic environment. You are driven by taking ownership, responsibility, optimalisation and collaboration. It is preferable that the candidate also has a strong analytical sense as well as having a strategic mindset to transform insights into initiatives.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eIn addition, you will need the following qualifications:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSolid experience within automotive aftersales, service network operations, or customer service management.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eRelevant degree in Business, Finance, Engineering, or equivalent professional experience.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience from the Polestar Service Network is considered a strong advantage.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDemonstrated ability to lead cross-functional projects and drive business and service improvements.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong data analysis capabilities with a track record of turning customer and operational insights into measurable results.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eIf you find the position interesting and the above description matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. Our selection process is ongoing, and the job advert will remain open until it’s filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":8040532},"datePosted":"2026-07-08T15:21:41+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":null,"addressLocality":"Oslo","postalCode":"0184","addressCountry":"NO","addressRegion":"Nordics \u0026 UK"}}]}},{"id":"7318b877-1044-4009-a022-875504bd2e4e","title":"Tax Manager I Global Direct Taxes","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/8036076-tax-manager-i-global-direct-taxes","date_published":"2026-07-08T09:07:17+02:00","content_html":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWe have an exciting opening at Polestar as Tax Manager who will be part of a fast-paced and challenging scale-up organization. You will play an important role in the Finance team supporting Polestar in its continued growth and expansion. In this finance role, you are a member of a dynamic and developing team. This role is key to further developing the Group Tax function at Polestar group. \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThis position is based in Polestar HQ, Gothenburg and reports directly to the Head of Group Tax. \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat you'll do \u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou will be part of the Group Tax team within Finance, working globally with direct taxes for the Polestar group. You will manage global tax processes, such as the group’s Pillar II reporting, as well as tax compliance, planning and strategy in accordance with applicable tax laws and regulations for certain Polestar legal entities. \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExamples of tasks are:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLead and drive the group’s Pillar II reporting\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDevelop and implement global tax strategies to optimize the group’s effective tax rate\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAdvise on tax implications of cross-border transactions and restructurings\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIdentify tax-saving opportunities and ensure alignment with business objectives\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eManage and ensure timely direct tax filings and payments\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eManage tax audits and inquiries from tax authorities\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eReview current and deferred tax calculations under local GAAP for certain Polestar legal entities\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMonitor and implement changes in local and global tax legislation \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eEnsure robust internal controls to mitigate direct tax risks\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLiaise with various internal and external stakeholders, such as colleagues in other Finance teams and other parts of the organisation, as well as with external advisors and auditors to ensure accurate tax reporting\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWho you are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eTo be successful in this role we think that you are a person with lots of energy, strong analytical skills together with an extensive experience in Swedish and International Tax law. You are a team player with the ability to propose, drive and implement improvements. You have a high level of accountability and commitment and can team up with various functions to engage in and drive projects and you can work independently and hands on in daily operations.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eOther important skills for this role:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eUniversity degree in Law or Finance or equivalent\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMinimum 8 years relevant work experience within tax, for example from the Swedish tax agency or the tax department of an audit firm or company \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience in Pillar II reporting is desirable\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eKnowledge of tax accounting and reporting is a merit\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFamiliarity with finance processes and systems is an advantage\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience from working in a regulated, publicly listed company environment is favourable but not a requirement\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePolestar is an international company, with various backgrounds represented. English, therefore, is the language of written and spoken communication. And though we have a global presence, we maintain the growth mindset. Change happens often at Polestar. But so does progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIf the above matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. Due to the summer holiday period, our recruitment process is moving at a slower pace, and we may not be able to provide updates in the meantime. We look forward to getting back to you during August.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Tax Manager I Global Direct Taxes","description":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWe have an exciting opening at Polestar as Tax Manager who will be part of a fast-paced and challenging scale-up organization. You will play an important role in the Finance team supporting Polestar in its continued growth and expansion. In this finance role, you are a member of a dynamic and developing team. This role is key to further developing the Group Tax function at Polestar group. \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThis position is based in Polestar HQ, Gothenburg and reports directly to the Head of Group Tax. \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat you'll do \u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou will be part of the Group Tax team within Finance, working globally with direct taxes for the Polestar group. You will manage global tax processes, such as the group’s Pillar II reporting, as well as tax compliance, planning and strategy in accordance with applicable tax laws and regulations for certain Polestar legal entities. \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExamples of tasks are:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLead and drive the group’s Pillar II reporting\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDevelop and implement global tax strategies to optimize the group’s effective tax rate\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAdvise on tax implications of cross-border transactions and restructurings\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIdentify tax-saving opportunities and ensure alignment with business objectives\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eManage and ensure timely direct tax filings and payments\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eManage tax audits and inquiries from tax authorities\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eReview current and deferred tax calculations under local GAAP for certain Polestar legal entities\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMonitor and implement changes in local and global tax legislation \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eEnsure robust internal controls to mitigate direct tax risks\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLiaise with various internal and external stakeholders, such as colleagues in other Finance teams and other parts of the organisation, as well as with external advisors and auditors to ensure accurate tax reporting\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWho you are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eTo be successful in this role we think that you are a person with lots of energy, strong analytical skills together with an extensive experience in Swedish and International Tax law. You are a team player with the ability to propose, drive and implement improvements. You have a high level of accountability and commitment and can team up with various functions to engage in and drive projects and you can work independently and hands on in daily operations.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eOther important skills for this role:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eUniversity degree in Law or Finance or equivalent\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMinimum 8 years relevant work experience within tax, for example from the Swedish tax agency or the tax department of an audit firm or company \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience in Pillar II reporting is desirable\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eKnowledge of tax accounting and reporting is a merit\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFamiliarity with finance processes and systems is an advantage\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience from working in a regulated, publicly listed company environment is favourable but not a requirement\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePolestar is an international company, with various backgrounds represented. English, therefore, is the language of written and spoken communication. And though we have a global presence, we maintain the growth mindset. Change happens often at Polestar. But so does progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIf the above matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. Due to the summer holiday period, our recruitment process is moving at a slower pace, and we may not be able to provide updates in the meantime. We look forward to getting back to you during August.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":8036076},"datePosted":"2026-07-08T09:07:17+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Assar Gabrielssons väg 9","addressLocality":"Göteborg","postalCode":"418 78","addressCountry":"SE","addressRegion":"Nordics \u0026 UK"}}]}},{"id":"c6ef45b7-c34b-4f1e-b7fe-4d650313b52c","title":"Liquidity Manager | Treasury Operations \u0026 Liquidity Analysis","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/8031989-liquidity-manager-treasury-operations-liquidity-analysis","date_published":"2026-07-07T15:42:19+02:00","content_html":"\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWe're currently looking for a Liquidity Manager to join our Treasury Operations \u0026amp; Liquidity Analysis team. In this role, you will be accountable for the overall cash flow health and liquidity position of both the Polestar Group and its individual legal entities. You will serve as the process owner for Group cash flow forecasting and reporting, ensuring transparency, accuracy, and actionable insights to support business decision-making.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eYou will work closely with internal stakeholders and external partners to support liquidity management, cash flow analysis, and financial risk mitigation. This is a role for someone who values structure and accuracy, enjoys working with complex financial flows, and is motivated by improving financial performance through strong cash and liquidity management practices. This position is located at Polestar HQ in Gothenburg, Sweden.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat You'll Do\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Liquidity Manager owns the end-to-end cash flow forecasting process, including governance, templates, reporting frameworks, and forecast quality. The position drives cash visibility, improves working capital efficiency, minimizes tied-up capital, and leads cross-functional actions to resolve liquidity challenges. Acting as the key partner and escalation point for Polestar Sales Units (PSUs), the Liquidity Manager ensures robust cash flow management practices and supports informed decision-making across the organization.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLiquidity \u0026amp; Cash Flow Management\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eOwn and manage the liquidity position of the Polestar Group and all legal entities within the Group.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eEnsure sufficient liquidity is available to support operational, strategic, and funding requirements.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMonitor short-, medium-, and long-term cash positions and proactively identify liquidity risks and opportunities.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDrive actions to improve overall cash flow health and resilience across the organization.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDevelop and maintain liquidity management frameworks, including funding, cash concentration, and cash optimization strategies.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDefine control procedures to secure there is no liquidity issues for the Polestar Group and all legal entities within the Group.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLead the resolution of complex cash flow issues that require coordination among headquarters functions, business functions, and Polestar Sales Units. \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFacilitate cross-functional discussions to identify root causes, remove barriers, and drive accountability. \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eEnsure timely execution of agreed actions and achievement of targeted outcomes.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCash Flow Forecasting\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eOwn the end-to-end direct cash flow forecasting process across the Group.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eBe accountable for the quality, accuracy, consolidation, and timely delivery of Group direct cash flow forecasts.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDefine, maintain, and continuously improve forecasting methodologies, templates, timelines, and governance frameworks.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDrive forecast accuracy through standardized processes, variance analysis, and challenge of underlying assumptions.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePartner with FP\u0026amp;A, Controlling, Accounting, Regional CFOs, the Shared Service Center, and other business functions to ensure reliable and actionable forecasts.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAct as the escalation point for Polestar Sales Units (PSUs) on cash flow forecasting-related matters, ensuring timely resolution and alignment.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eReporting \u0026amp; Cash Visibility\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eOwn Group cash flow reporting and provide management with transparent and timely visibility of cash positions, forecast performance, and liquidity risks.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eImplement and continuously enhance reporting frameworks that provide real-time visibility of cash and liquidity status across the Group.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDevelop and maintain dashboards, KPIs, and management reports to support decision-making at both operational and executive levels.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eProvide insightful analysis on liquidity trends, forecast deviations, working capital developments, and funding requirements.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDrive continuous improvements in reporting quality, automation, and process efficiency.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCapital Efficiency\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDrive initiatives to minimize tied-up capital and optimize working capital performance across the Group.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIdentify structural performance gaps, develop business cases, define action plans, and coordinate cross-functional execution to achieve targeted KPI improvements.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eTrack, report, and validate the financial impact of improvement initiatives, ensuring sustainable benefits are embedded into business operations where applicable.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMonitor and report progress against cash flow and liquidity targets.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStrategic KPI Improvement Initiatives\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIdentify opportunities to improve cash flow, liquidity, forecast accuracy, and working capital performance.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLead and deliver one-time initiatives to drive measurable improvements in key cash flow, and liquidity KPIs.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAnalyze performance gaps, define action plans, and coordinate cross-functional stakeholders to ensure successful implementation.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eTrack, validate, and communicate the impact of initiatives against agreed targets and KPIs.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eChallenge existing processes and drive continuous improvement through best practices in cash management and forecasting.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAct as a catalyst for continuous improvement by identifying and delivering targeted actions to address underperforming areas.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWho You Are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eTo succeed in this role, and at Polestar in general, you'll need tenacity, flexibility, and curiosity. The ability to take initiative, meet deadlines, and adapt to changing priorities is essential. You are analytical and structured, with a strong understanding of liquidity and cash flow dynamics. You communicate effectively across functions and cultures, challenge the status quo when needed, and enjoy turning financial insights into tangible business actions.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn addition, we believe you have these qualifications:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eBachelor's degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, Business Administration, or a related field.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e7+ years of experience in Treasury, Liquidity Management, Corporate Finance, Cash Management, FP\u0026amp;A, or related disciplines.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMinimum 5 years of experience within the automotive industry.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eProven experience managing liquidity and cash flow forecasting in a multinational environment with multiple legal entities.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong expertise in cash flow forecasting, liquidity management, and working capital optimization.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience implementing reporting frameworks, dashboards, and performance management processes.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDemonstrated ability to lead cross-functional initiatives and influence stakeholders at all organizational levels.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience working with ERP and Treasury Management Systems.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAdvanced analytical and financial modeling skills.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eGood knowledge of cash pooling structures, in-house banking, FX risk management, and cash management processes is highly desirable.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFamiliarity with banking platforms is advantageous.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePolestar is an international company, with various backgrounds represented. English is the language of written and spoken communication. While we are global, we maintain a growth mindset. Change happens often at Polestar, but so does progress. Expect an accelerating and exciting environment.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIf the above matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. Due to the summer holiday period, our recruitment process is moving at a slower pace, and we may not be able to provide updates in the meantime. We look forward to getting back to you during August.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Liquidity Manager | Treasury Operations \u0026 Liquidity Analysis","description":"\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWe're currently looking for a Liquidity Manager to join our Treasury Operations \u0026amp; Liquidity Analysis team. In this role, you will be accountable for the overall cash flow health and liquidity position of both the Polestar Group and its individual legal entities. You will serve as the process owner for Group cash flow forecasting and reporting, ensuring transparency, accuracy, and actionable insights to support business decision-making.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eYou will work closely with internal stakeholders and external partners to support liquidity management, cash flow analysis, and financial risk mitigation. This is a role for someone who values structure and accuracy, enjoys working with complex financial flows, and is motivated by improving financial performance through strong cash and liquidity management practices. This position is located at Polestar HQ in Gothenburg, Sweden.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat You'll Do\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Liquidity Manager owns the end-to-end cash flow forecasting process, including governance, templates, reporting frameworks, and forecast quality. The position drives cash visibility, improves working capital efficiency, minimizes tied-up capital, and leads cross-functional actions to resolve liquidity challenges. Acting as the key partner and escalation point for Polestar Sales Units (PSUs), the Liquidity Manager ensures robust cash flow management practices and supports informed decision-making across the organization.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLiquidity \u0026amp; Cash Flow Management\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eOwn and manage the liquidity position of the Polestar Group and all legal entities within the Group.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eEnsure sufficient liquidity is available to support operational, strategic, and funding requirements.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMonitor short-, medium-, and long-term cash positions and proactively identify liquidity risks and opportunities.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDrive actions to improve overall cash flow health and resilience across the organization.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDevelop and maintain liquidity management frameworks, including funding, cash concentration, and cash optimization strategies.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDefine control procedures to secure there is no liquidity issues for the Polestar Group and all legal entities within the Group.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLead the resolution of complex cash flow issues that require coordination among headquarters functions, business functions, and Polestar Sales Units. \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFacilitate cross-functional discussions to identify root causes, remove barriers, and drive accountability. \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eEnsure timely execution of agreed actions and achievement of targeted outcomes.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCash Flow Forecasting\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eOwn the end-to-end direct cash flow forecasting process across the Group.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eBe accountable for the quality, accuracy, consolidation, and timely delivery of Group direct cash flow forecasts.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDefine, maintain, and continuously improve forecasting methodologies, templates, timelines, and governance frameworks.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDrive forecast accuracy through standardized processes, variance analysis, and challenge of underlying assumptions.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePartner with FP\u0026amp;A, Controlling, Accounting, Regional CFOs, the Shared Service Center, and other business functions to ensure reliable and actionable forecasts.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAct as the escalation point for Polestar Sales Units (PSUs) on cash flow forecasting-related matters, ensuring timely resolution and alignment.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eReporting \u0026amp; Cash Visibility\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eOwn Group cash flow reporting and provide management with transparent and timely visibility of cash positions, forecast performance, and liquidity risks.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eImplement and continuously enhance reporting frameworks that provide real-time visibility of cash and liquidity status across the Group.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDevelop and maintain dashboards, KPIs, and management reports to support decision-making at both operational and executive levels.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eProvide insightful analysis on liquidity trends, forecast deviations, working capital developments, and funding requirements.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDrive continuous improvements in reporting quality, automation, and process efficiency.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCapital Efficiency\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDrive initiatives to minimize tied-up capital and optimize working capital performance across the Group.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIdentify structural performance gaps, develop business cases, define action plans, and coordinate cross-functional execution to achieve targeted KPI improvements.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eTrack, report, and validate the financial impact of improvement initiatives, ensuring sustainable benefits are embedded into business operations where applicable.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMonitor and report progress against cash flow and liquidity targets.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStrategic KPI Improvement Initiatives\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIdentify opportunities to improve cash flow, liquidity, forecast accuracy, and working capital performance.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLead and deliver one-time initiatives to drive measurable improvements in key cash flow, and liquidity KPIs.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAnalyze performance gaps, define action plans, and coordinate cross-functional stakeholders to ensure successful implementation.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eTrack, validate, and communicate the impact of initiatives against agreed targets and KPIs.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eChallenge existing processes and drive continuous improvement through best practices in cash management and forecasting.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAct as a catalyst for continuous improvement by identifying and delivering targeted actions to address underperforming areas.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWho You Are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eTo succeed in this role, and at Polestar in general, you'll need tenacity, flexibility, and curiosity. The ability to take initiative, meet deadlines, and adapt to changing priorities is essential. You are analytical and structured, with a strong understanding of liquidity and cash flow dynamics. You communicate effectively across functions and cultures, challenge the status quo when needed, and enjoy turning financial insights into tangible business actions.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn addition, we believe you have these qualifications:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eBachelor's degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, Business Administration, or a related field.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e7+ years of experience in Treasury, Liquidity Management, Corporate Finance, Cash Management, FP\u0026amp;A, or related disciplines.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMinimum 5 years of experience within the automotive industry.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eProven experience managing liquidity and cash flow forecasting in a multinational environment with multiple legal entities.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong expertise in cash flow forecasting, liquidity management, and working capital optimization.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience implementing reporting frameworks, dashboards, and performance management processes.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDemonstrated ability to lead cross-functional initiatives and influence stakeholders at all organizational levels.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience working with ERP and Treasury Management Systems.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAdvanced analytical and financial modeling skills.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eGood knowledge of cash pooling structures, in-house banking, FX risk management, and cash management processes is highly desirable.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFamiliarity with banking platforms is advantageous.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePolestar is an international company, with various backgrounds represented. English is the language of written and spoken communication. While we are global, we maintain a growth mindset. Change happens often at Polestar, but so does progress. Expect an accelerating and exciting environment.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIf the above matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. Due to the summer holiday period, our recruitment process is moving at a slower pace, and we may not be able to provide updates in the meantime. We look forward to getting back to you during August.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":8031989},"datePosted":"2026-07-07T15:42:19+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Assar Gabrielssons väg 9","addressLocality":"Göteborg","postalCode":"418 78","addressCountry":"SE","addressRegion":"Nordics \u0026 UK"}}]}},{"id":"b0fe4652-1524-4089-b642-301d4822b559","title":"Commercial Planning Manager | South Korea","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/8028271-commercial-planning-manager-south-korea","date_published":"2026-07-07T09:48:05+02:00","content_html":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWe're currently looking for a Commercial Planning Manager to join our Commercial Operations team and deliver strong business planning and customer journey management capabilities. This role is responsible for sales volume planning, digital customer journey, payment operations and various business reporting to support sustainable business growth and operational excellence.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThis position is located at Polestar Automotive Korea office in Gangnam-gu, Seoul. We believe in a hybrid model when it comes to remote and onsite work, knowing that both in-person collaboration and individual time to focus are needed. What matters most is that people get the time, and support, to do what needs to be done. And to enjoy doing it, of course.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe responsibilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe Commercial Planning Manager will be responsible for planning sales volume and managing customer journeys, digital operations and business reporting to support commercial performance. This role will directly report to Head of Commercial Operations.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat you'll do\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDevelop monthly sales volume plans and manage sales forecasts, including order intake, product mix, option mix and business outlook.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eManage the end-to-end digital customer journey and related systems to continuously improve customer experience and operational efficiency.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDrive financial product management and tactical campaigns based on market trends and budgets, while supervising partner alignments (FSP, credit card company and PG) and weekly/monthly performance reviews with HQ.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAct as the primary point of contact for customer journey and digital sales process issues, coordinating with relevant team in HQ / APAC and internal stakeholders to ensure timely resolution and continuous process improvement.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eManage business operations related to payment, Mo2 and EV subsidy processes while coordinating with internal stakeholders and external partners.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMonitor commercial performance and prepare regular business planning reports, forecasts and presentations for HQ and management.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSupport new model launches by ensuring customer journey, digital operations and commercial process readiness.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIdentify opportunities to improve commercial processes through data analysis, system enhancements and cross-functional collaboration\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWho you are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWe seek a highly motivated and analytical team player with strong commercial planning capabilities and a structured approach to problem-solving. You are comfortable managing multiple priorities, working with cross-functional stakeholders, and translating data into actionable business insights. In addition, you'll need the following qualifications:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMaster or Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Economics, Marketing or equivalent\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMinimum 6 years’ experience in the automotive field or related\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong analytical skills with the ability to translate data into business insights and recommendation\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience in business planning, forecasting and performance reporting\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience in managing cross-functional projects and driving process improvements\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong stakeholder management skills\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExcellent written and verbal English skills\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that a change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate-neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative. Together, we are creating, collaborating and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs this you?\u003c/strong\u003e If you are interested in joining the Polestar crew, don't wait with submitting your application. We apply a continuous selection process and the job post will be open until the position is filled.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric by the way...\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Commercial Planning Manager | South Korea","description":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWe're currently looking for a Commercial Planning Manager to join our Commercial Operations team and deliver strong business planning and customer journey management capabilities. This role is responsible for sales volume planning, digital customer journey, payment operations and various business reporting to support sustainable business growth and operational excellence.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThis position is located at Polestar Automotive Korea office in Gangnam-gu, Seoul. We believe in a hybrid model when it comes to remote and onsite work, knowing that both in-person collaboration and individual time to focus are needed. What matters most is that people get the time, and support, to do what needs to be done. And to enjoy doing it, of course.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe responsibilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe Commercial Planning Manager will be responsible for planning sales volume and managing customer journeys, digital operations and business reporting to support commercial performance. This role will directly report to Head of Commercial Operations.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat you'll do\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDevelop monthly sales volume plans and manage sales forecasts, including order intake, product mix, option mix and business outlook.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eManage the end-to-end digital customer journey and related systems to continuously improve customer experience and operational efficiency.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDrive financial product management and tactical campaigns based on market trends and budgets, while supervising partner alignments (FSP, credit card company and PG) and weekly/monthly performance reviews with HQ.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAct as the primary point of contact for customer journey and digital sales process issues, coordinating with relevant team in HQ / APAC and internal stakeholders to ensure timely resolution and continuous process improvement.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eManage business operations related to payment, Mo2 and EV subsidy processes while coordinating with internal stakeholders and external partners.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMonitor commercial performance and prepare regular business planning reports, forecasts and presentations for HQ and management.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSupport new model launches by ensuring customer journey, digital operations and commercial process readiness.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIdentify opportunities to improve commercial processes through data analysis, system enhancements and cross-functional collaboration\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWho you are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWe seek a highly motivated and analytical team player with strong commercial planning capabilities and a structured approach to problem-solving. You are comfortable managing multiple priorities, working with cross-functional stakeholders, and translating data into actionable business insights. In addition, you'll need the following qualifications:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMaster or Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Economics, Marketing or equivalent\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMinimum 6 years’ experience in the automotive field or related\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong analytical skills with the ability to translate data into business insights and recommendation\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience in business planning, forecasting and performance reporting\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExperience in managing cross-functional projects and driving process improvements\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStrong stakeholder management skills\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExcellent written and verbal English skills\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that a change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate-neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative. Together, we are creating, collaborating and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs this you?\u003c/strong\u003e If you are interested in joining the Polestar crew, don't wait with submitting your application. We apply a continuous selection process and the job post will be open until the position is filled.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric by the way...\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":8028271},"datePosted":"2026-07-07T09:48:05+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":null,"addressLocality":"Seoul","postalCode":"100-101","addressCountry":"KR","addressRegion":"APEC"}}]}},{"id":"342ebaf8-5921-4252-9e32-f374e41d4e56","title":"Senior Software Developer","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/7978713-senior-software-developer","date_published":"2026-07-07T00:00:00+02:00","content_html":"\u003ch4\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is accelerating the transition to sustainable mobility through electric performance. Behind that journey sits a powerful digital platform enabling everything from checkout and payments to order management, delivery, retail tools, and customer self‑service.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAt Polestar Digital, we build innovative, scalable solutions that power our global platform. You will join a focused team working across a critical part of the customer journey, delivering systems that customers globally and hundreds of internal users depend on every day. With real ownership, close collaboration, and global impact, you will play a key role in shaping the future of Polestar’s digital ecosystem.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are now looking for a Senior Software Developer to join our headquarters in Gothenburg, Sweden.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs a Senior Software Developer, you will be part of a cross‑functional agile team responsible for designing and building high‑performance, scalable solutions that support Polestar’s global digital platform.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will take ownership of system architecture and technical decision‑making while working closely with Product Managers, Designers, and Operations teams to deliver reliable and impactful solutions. The role combines hands‑on development, system design, and collaboration, while also contributing to a strong engineering culture through mentoring and knowledge‑sharing.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will write clean, well‑tested code and contribute to building systems that are robust, scalable, and maintainable. At the same time, you will stay up to date with modern development practices and emerging technologies, including evolving paradigms such as agentic AI.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eWhat you'll do\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will design, build, and evolve scalable digital solutions that power Polestar’s global platform.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYour responsibilities include:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDesigning and implementing high‑performance, globally scalable systems\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eTaking ownership of system architecture and contributing to technical decision‑making\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eWriting clean, maintainable code supported by unit, integration, and automated tests\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eCollaborating closely with Product Managers, Designers, and Operations teams to deliver business value\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMentoring team members and contributing to a culture of knowledge‑sharing\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEnsuring solutions follow modern engineering practices across quality, performance, and maintainability\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn your daily work, you will collaborate closely with cross‑functional agile teams including engineering, product, design, and operations, contributing to a shared understanding of system design, user impact, and business priorities.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eWho you are\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou are an experienced software developer with a strong engineering foundation and a passion for building scalable, high‑quality systems. You are comfortable taking ownership of technical challenges, making decisions, and collaborating across teams to deliver impactful solutions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou combine strong technical skills with a product mindset, understanding not only how to build solutions but also why they matter. You enjoy sharing knowledge, supporting others, and continuously improving both code and ways of working.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTo be a great fit for this position, we believe you have:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong knowledge of programming and software engineering principles\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience designing scalable systems using .NET (C#), AWS, and Node.js (TypeScript)\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDemonstrated ability to write effective unit tests, integration tests, and other automated tests\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSolid understanding of DevOps practices, CI/CD pipelines, and containerization\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eProficiency with version control systems such as Git and GitHub workflows\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e4–8 years of professional software development experience\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience building global, high‑performance, and scalable solutions\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience working in cross‑functional agile teams\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong problem‑solving skills with the ability to process and analyze complex information\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eFluency in English, both written and spoken\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eIt is considered an advantage if you also have:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience working in the financial domain\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eInterest in emerging technologies, including agentic AI, and how they impact software development\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch4\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that a change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate‑neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTogether, we are creating, collaborating, and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility. We are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eIs this you?\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf you are interested in joining the Polestar crew, don’t wait to submit your application. We apply a continuous selection process and the job post will remain open until the position is filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf this sounds like your next challenge, please submit your resume, portfolio, or GitHub profile along with a brief note about what excites you about joining Polestar.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs we move through the Swedish summer holiday season, there may be a slight delay in our process. We look forward to getting back to you in August.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric, by the way…\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Senior Software Developer","description":"\u003ch4\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is accelerating the transition to sustainable mobility through electric performance. Behind that journey sits a powerful digital platform enabling everything from checkout and payments to order management, delivery, retail tools, and customer self‑service.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAt Polestar Digital, we build innovative, scalable solutions that power our global platform. You will join a focused team working across a critical part of the customer journey, delivering systems that customers globally and hundreds of internal users depend on every day. With real ownership, close collaboration, and global impact, you will play a key role in shaping the future of Polestar’s digital ecosystem.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are now looking for a Senior Software Developer to join our headquarters in Gothenburg, Sweden.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs a Senior Software Developer, you will be part of a cross‑functional agile team responsible for designing and building high‑performance, scalable solutions that support Polestar’s global digital platform.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will take ownership of system architecture and technical decision‑making while working closely with Product Managers, Designers, and Operations teams to deliver reliable and impactful solutions. The role combines hands‑on development, system design, and collaboration, while also contributing to a strong engineering culture through mentoring and knowledge‑sharing.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will write clean, well‑tested code and contribute to building systems that are robust, scalable, and maintainable. At the same time, you will stay up to date with modern development practices and emerging technologies, including evolving paradigms such as agentic AI.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eWhat you'll do\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will design, build, and evolve scalable digital solutions that power Polestar’s global platform.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYour responsibilities include:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDesigning and implementing high‑performance, globally scalable systems\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eTaking ownership of system architecture and contributing to technical decision‑making\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eWriting clean, maintainable code supported by unit, integration, and automated tests\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eCollaborating closely with Product Managers, Designers, and Operations teams to deliver business value\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMentoring team members and contributing to a culture of knowledge‑sharing\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEnsuring solutions follow modern engineering practices across quality, performance, and maintainability\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn your daily work, you will collaborate closely with cross‑functional agile teams including engineering, product, design, and operations, contributing to a shared understanding of system design, user impact, and business priorities.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eWho you are\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou are an experienced software developer with a strong engineering foundation and a passion for building scalable, high‑quality systems. You are comfortable taking ownership of technical challenges, making decisions, and collaborating across teams to deliver impactful solutions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou combine strong technical skills with a product mindset, understanding not only how to build solutions but also why they matter. You enjoy sharing knowledge, supporting others, and continuously improving both code and ways of working.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTo be a great fit for this position, we believe you have:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong knowledge of programming and software engineering principles\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience designing scalable systems using .NET (C#), AWS, and Node.js (TypeScript)\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDemonstrated ability to write effective unit tests, integration tests, and other automated tests\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSolid understanding of DevOps practices, CI/CD pipelines, and containerization\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eProficiency with version control systems such as Git and GitHub workflows\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e4–8 years of professional software development experience\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience building global, high‑performance, and scalable solutions\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience working in cross‑functional agile teams\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong problem‑solving skills with the ability to process and analyze complex information\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eFluency in English, both written and spoken\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eIt is considered an advantage if you also have:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience working in the financial domain\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eInterest in emerging technologies, including agentic AI, and how they impact software development\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch4\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that a change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate‑neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTogether, we are creating, collaborating, and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility. We are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eIs this you?\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf you are interested in joining the Polestar crew, don’t wait to submit your application. We apply a continuous selection process and the job post will remain open until the position is filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf this sounds like your next challenge, please submit your resume, portfolio, or GitHub profile along with a brief note about what excites you about joining Polestar.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs we move through the Swedish summer holiday season, there may be a slight delay in our process. We look forward to getting back to you in August.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric, by the way…\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":7978713},"datePosted":"2026-07-07T00:00:00+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Assar Gabrielssons väg 9","addressLocality":"Göteborg","postalCode":"418 78","addressCountry":"SE","addressRegion":"Nordics \u0026 UK"}}]}},{"id":"9b8c5ffe-852c-4556-b880-627c8e61335e","title":"Senior Solution Architect","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/7992513-senior-solution-architect","date_published":"2026-07-02T00:00:00+02:00","content_html":"\u003ch4\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is accelerating the transition to sustainable mobility through electric performance. Car Services and Industrial Operations is a newly established area that plays a vital role in Polestar’s business.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eOur mission is to ensure that Polestar can offer services to customers seamlessly, while giving our service partners the digital tools they need to enhance, maintain, and repair our vehicles. We support compound operations so that cars are properly prepared and delivered to their owners on time. We also collect, analyze, and share data that provides valuable product insights, helping the quality organization to quickly identify and resolve issues, keeping customers satisfied and reducing quality costs.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eProduct compliance is another cornerstone of our work, ensuring that Polestar’s products meet both new and existing legislation across all markets where we operate. In addition, we support contract manufacturing by enabling downstream processes such as homologation, Certification of Conformity, and warranty handling.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eSustainability is at the heart of what we do. Through smart digital solutions, we contribute to Polestar’s vision of a more sustainable future by making key data accessible across manufacturing, logistics, aftermarket, and sustainability, empowering better decisions, streamlined operations, and an elevated customer experience.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are a close‑knit and experienced team. Several of us have worked together for a long time, creating a cohesive environment built on collaboration and mutual support. We are ambitious, set high standards, and strive to deliver outstanding solutions, while remaining prestige‑free, adaptable, and focused on the customer.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are now looking for a Senior Solution Architect to join us at our headquarters in Gothenburg, Sweden.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs a Senior Solution Architect, you will guide multiple teams in building aligned, scalable, and high‑quality solutions across the Car Services and Industrial Operations.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will work across teams, systems, and organizational boundaries, ensuring that solutions are aligned with enterprise architecture while supporting business needs. The role combines architecture leadership, technical direction, and cross‑functional collaboration, where you will contribute to shaping both current and future digital capabilities.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will act as a key partner to product and technology leadership, helping teams make the right architectural decisions while driving standardization, reducing complexity, and enabling long‑term scalability.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eWhat you'll do\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will lead architecture across multiple teams and ensure that solutions are scalable, aligned, and built for long‑term success.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYour responsibilities include:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eLeading architecture across several teams within Car Services and Industrial Operations\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEnsuring solutions align with enterprise architecture principles and standards\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSupporting teams with technology strategy, cloud architecture, and DevOps practices\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDesigning solutions that are scalable, cost‑efficient, and global by design\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eResolving cross‑team technical challenges and removing impediments\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAligning product roadmaps with target architecture together with product and technology leadership\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEnsuring security, compliance, and risk considerations are embedded in solutions\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDriving standardization and reducing fragmentation across teams\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eManaging and reducing technical debt at area level\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDefining reusable patterns, APIs, and integration approaches\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eCoordinating integrations and dependencies across systems and teams\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eContributing to the broader architecture community\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn your daily work, you will collaborate closely with product and engineering teams across Car Services and Industrial Operations, as well as business stakeholders within service, customer experience, and operations, ensuring that architecture supports both technical and business outcomes. You will also work with the broader architecture community, including Solution Architects, Chief Architects, and Enterprise Architects, together with leadership and external partners where relevant.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eWho you are\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou enjoy working across teams and systems, solving complex problems, and bringing structure to large‑scale environments. You are comfortable working with both technical teams and business stakeholders, and you can explain complex topics in a clear and practical way.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou combine strong technical understanding with the ability to connect strategy, architecture, and execution, and you are motivated by enabling teams to deliver scalable and high‑quality solutions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTo be a great fit for this position, we believe you have:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience designing solutions across multiple teams or domains\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong knowledge of cloud platforms, CI/CD, and modern system architecture\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience working with integrations, APIs, and distributed systems\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience delivering solutions across organizational and business boundaries\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong understanding of non‑functional requirements such as security, performance, and availability\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience standardizing solutions and managing dependencies and technical debt\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAt least 5 years of experience in solution architecture\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience within automotive, mobility, or service‑based digital platforms is considered a strong advantage.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that a change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate‑neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTogether, we are creating, collaborating, and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility. We are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eIs this you?\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf this sounds like the right challenge for you, we encourage you to apply. We apply a continuous selection process, and the position will remain open until filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs we move through the Swedish summer holiday season, there may be a slight delay in our process. We look forward to getting back to you in August.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric, by the way…\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Senior Solution Architect","description":"\u003ch4\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is accelerating the transition to sustainable mobility through electric performance. Car Services and Industrial Operations is a newly established area that plays a vital role in Polestar’s business.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eOur mission is to ensure that Polestar can offer services to customers seamlessly, while giving our service partners the digital tools they need to enhance, maintain, and repair our vehicles. We support compound operations so that cars are properly prepared and delivered to their owners on time. We also collect, analyze, and share data that provides valuable product insights, helping the quality organization to quickly identify and resolve issues, keeping customers satisfied and reducing quality costs.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eProduct compliance is another cornerstone of our work, ensuring that Polestar’s products meet both new and existing legislation across all markets where we operate. In addition, we support contract manufacturing by enabling downstream processes such as homologation, Certification of Conformity, and warranty handling.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eSustainability is at the heart of what we do. Through smart digital solutions, we contribute to Polestar’s vision of a more sustainable future by making key data accessible across manufacturing, logistics, aftermarket, and sustainability, empowering better decisions, streamlined operations, and an elevated customer experience.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are a close‑knit and experienced team. Several of us have worked together for a long time, creating a cohesive environment built on collaboration and mutual support. We are ambitious, set high standards, and strive to deliver outstanding solutions, while remaining prestige‑free, adaptable, and focused on the customer.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are now looking for a Senior Solution Architect to join us at our headquarters in Gothenburg, Sweden.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs a Senior Solution Architect, you will guide multiple teams in building aligned, scalable, and high‑quality solutions across the Car Services and Industrial Operations.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will work across teams, systems, and organizational boundaries, ensuring that solutions are aligned with enterprise architecture while supporting business needs. The role combines architecture leadership, technical direction, and cross‑functional collaboration, where you will contribute to shaping both current and future digital capabilities.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will act as a key partner to product and technology leadership, helping teams make the right architectural decisions while driving standardization, reducing complexity, and enabling long‑term scalability.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eWhat you'll do\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will lead architecture across multiple teams and ensure that solutions are scalable, aligned, and built for long‑term success.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYour responsibilities include:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eLeading architecture across several teams within Car Services and Industrial Operations\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEnsuring solutions align with enterprise architecture principles and standards\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSupporting teams with technology strategy, cloud architecture, and DevOps practices\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDesigning solutions that are scalable, cost‑efficient, and global by design\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eResolving cross‑team technical challenges and removing impediments\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAligning product roadmaps with target architecture together with product and technology leadership\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEnsuring security, compliance, and risk considerations are embedded in solutions\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDriving standardization and reducing fragmentation across teams\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eManaging and reducing technical debt at area level\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDefining reusable patterns, APIs, and integration approaches\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eCoordinating integrations and dependencies across systems and teams\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eContributing to the broader architecture community\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn your daily work, you will collaborate closely with product and engineering teams across Car Services and Industrial Operations, as well as business stakeholders within service, customer experience, and operations, ensuring that architecture supports both technical and business outcomes. You will also work with the broader architecture community, including Solution Architects, Chief Architects, and Enterprise Architects, together with leadership and external partners where relevant.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eWho you are\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou enjoy working across teams and systems, solving complex problems, and bringing structure to large‑scale environments. You are comfortable working with both technical teams and business stakeholders, and you can explain complex topics in a clear and practical way.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou combine strong technical understanding with the ability to connect strategy, architecture, and execution, and you are motivated by enabling teams to deliver scalable and high‑quality solutions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTo be a great fit for this position, we believe you have:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience designing solutions across multiple teams or domains\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong knowledge of cloud platforms, CI/CD, and modern system architecture\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience working with integrations, APIs, and distributed systems\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience delivering solutions across organizational and business boundaries\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong understanding of non‑functional requirements such as security, performance, and availability\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience standardizing solutions and managing dependencies and technical debt\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAt least 5 years of experience in solution architecture\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience within automotive, mobility, or service‑based digital platforms is considered a strong advantage.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that a change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate‑neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTogether, we are creating, collaborating, and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility. We are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eIs this you?\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf this sounds like the right challenge for you, we encourage you to apply. We apply a continuous selection process, and the position will remain open until filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs we move through the Swedish summer holiday season, there may be a slight delay in our process. We look forward to getting back to you in August.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric, by the way…\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":7992513},"datePosted":"2026-07-02T00:00:00+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Assar Gabrielssons väg 9","addressLocality":"Göteborg","postalCode":"418 78","addressCountry":"SE","addressRegion":"Nordics \u0026 UK"}}]}},{"id":"b9edc308-d424-4e3b-a5c2-f9f329a31c97","title":"Senior Quality Assurance Engineer","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/7973296-senior-quality-assurance-engineer","date_published":"2026-06-25T16:18:46+02:00","content_html":"\u003ch4\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is accelerating the transition to sustainable mobility through electric performance. Behind that journey sits a powerful digital platform enabling everything from checkout and payments to order management, delivery, retail tools, and customer self‑service.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will join a focused team working across a critical part of the customer journey, building and validating solutions that customers globally and hundreds of internal users depend on every day. With real ownership, close collaboration, and global impact, this role plays a key part in ensuring reliability, performance, and quality across Polestar’s digital ecosystem.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are now looking for a Senior Quality Assurance Engineer to join Polestar Digital at our headquarters in Gothenburg, Sweden.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs a Senior Quality Assurance Engineer, you will ensure the reliability, performance, and quality of customer‑facing digital products and internal platforms that support the vehicle purchasing journey.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will work across frontend, backend, APIs, and cloud infrastructure, validating solutions and ensuring that features meet both business and technical requirements before release. Acting as a key partner to Software Engineers, Product Managers, Designers, and Operations teams, you will translate product requirements into effective test strategies and ensure that defects are identified early and resolved efficiently.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe role combines hands‑on testing, automation, and continuous improvement of quality practices, contributing to scalable and high‑quality systems used globally across markets and internal operations. You will also stay up to date with modern QA methodologies and emerging technologies, including AI‑assisted testing approaches.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eWhat you'll do\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will ensure high‑quality delivery across Polestar’s digital platforms by validating solutions, improving test coverage, and driving continuous improvement in quality practices.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYour responsibilities include:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEnsuring business requirements and acceptance criteria are fulfilled through comprehensive testing of user stories and system workflows\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDesigning, executing, and maintaining manual and automated tests across frontend, backend, APIs, and integrations\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eValidating quality, reliability, performance, and security of new platform capabilities and releases\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eCollaborating with Software Engineers, Technical Leads, Product Managers, and Designers to translate product requirements into effective test strategies\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIdentifying, documenting, prioritizing, and tracking defects, while supporting teams in root‑cause analysis and resolution\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eContributing to test automation frameworks and improving overall test coverage and development practices\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eWorking closely with cross‑functional agile teams to continuously improve software quality and delivery processes\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMonitoring and evaluating quality metrics and contributing to continuous improvement initiatives\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStaying up to date with industry best practices, modern QA methodologies, and emerging technologies, including AI‑assisted testing approaches\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDocumenting test plans, test results, and quality standards across the development lifecycle\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn your daily work, you will collaborate closely with Software Engineers, Product Managers, Designers, Technical Leads, and Operations teams, ensuring alignment across technical and business needs while driving quality across the full development lifecycle.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eWho you are\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou are a structured and analytical quality professional with strong ownership and a proactive approach to ensuring high‑quality outcomes. You are comfortable working independently while collaborating closely with cross‑functional teams, and you focus on identifying and resolving issues early to enable smooth and reliable delivery.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou combine hands‑on testing expertise with a continuous improvement mindset and an interest in modern technologies shaping the future of software quality.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTo be a great fit for this position, we believe you have:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong knowledge and hands‑on experience with Quality Assurance methodologies and software testing principles\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience testing modern web applications and distributed systems across frontend and backend technologies\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience with test automation tools and frameworks for UI, API, and integration testing\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eUnderstanding of React, TypeScript, .NET (C#), Node.js, APIs, and AWS‑based systems from a testing perspective\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience working with CI/CD pipelines, GitHub workflows, and containerized environments\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eKnowledge of Agile development methodologies and experience working in cross‑functional product teams\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong analytical, organizational, problem‑solving, and communication skills\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAbility to work independently while collaborating effectively across teams and stakeholders\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience with commerce, payments, financing, order management, or customer journey platforms is considered an advantage\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAtleast 4 years of professional experience in Software Quality Assurance\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that a change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate‑neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTogether, we are creating, collaborating, and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility. We are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eIs this you?\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf you are interested in joining the Polestar crew, don’t wait to submit your application. We apply a continuous selection process and the job post will remain open until the position is filled.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAs we move through the Swedish summer holiday season, there may be a slight delay in our process. We look forward to getting back to you in August.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eSend us your resume along with a short note on what makes this role interesting to you. We read everything.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric, by the way…\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Senior Quality Assurance Engineer","description":"\u003ch4\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is accelerating the transition to sustainable mobility through electric performance. Behind that journey sits a powerful digital platform enabling everything from checkout and payments to order management, delivery, retail tools, and customer self‑service.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will join a focused team working across a critical part of the customer journey, building and validating solutions that customers globally and hundreds of internal users depend on every day. With real ownership, close collaboration, and global impact, this role plays a key part in ensuring reliability, performance, and quality across Polestar’s digital ecosystem.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are now looking for a Senior Quality Assurance Engineer to join Polestar Digital at our headquarters in Gothenburg, Sweden.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs a Senior Quality Assurance Engineer, you will ensure the reliability, performance, and quality of customer‑facing digital products and internal platforms that support the vehicle purchasing journey.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will work across frontend, backend, APIs, and cloud infrastructure, validating solutions and ensuring that features meet both business and technical requirements before release. Acting as a key partner to Software Engineers, Product Managers, Designers, and Operations teams, you will translate product requirements into effective test strategies and ensure that defects are identified early and resolved efficiently.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe role combines hands‑on testing, automation, and continuous improvement of quality practices, contributing to scalable and high‑quality systems used globally across markets and internal operations. You will also stay up to date with modern QA methodologies and emerging technologies, including AI‑assisted testing approaches.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eWhat you'll do\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou will ensure high‑quality delivery across Polestar’s digital platforms by validating solutions, improving test coverage, and driving continuous improvement in quality practices.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYour responsibilities include:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEnsuring business requirements and acceptance criteria are fulfilled through comprehensive testing of user stories and system workflows\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDesigning, executing, and maintaining manual and automated tests across frontend, backend, APIs, and integrations\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eValidating quality, reliability, performance, and security of new platform capabilities and releases\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eCollaborating with Software Engineers, Technical Leads, Product Managers, and Designers to translate product requirements into effective test strategies\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIdentifying, documenting, prioritizing, and tracking defects, while supporting teams in root‑cause analysis and resolution\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eContributing to test automation frameworks and improving overall test coverage and development practices\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eWorking closely with cross‑functional agile teams to continuously improve software quality and delivery processes\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMonitoring and evaluating quality metrics and contributing to continuous improvement initiatives\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStaying up to date with industry best practices, modern QA methodologies, and emerging technologies, including AI‑assisted testing approaches\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDocumenting test plans, test results, and quality standards across the development lifecycle\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn your daily work, you will collaborate closely with Software Engineers, Product Managers, Designers, Technical Leads, and Operations teams, ensuring alignment across technical and business needs while driving quality across the full development lifecycle.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eWho you are\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou are a structured and analytical quality professional with strong ownership and a proactive approach to ensuring high‑quality outcomes. You are comfortable working independently while collaborating closely with cross‑functional teams, and you focus on identifying and resolving issues early to enable smooth and reliable delivery.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou combine hands‑on testing expertise with a continuous improvement mindset and an interest in modern technologies shaping the future of software quality.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTo be a great fit for this position, we believe you have:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong knowledge and hands‑on experience with Quality Assurance methodologies and software testing principles\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience testing modern web applications and distributed systems across frontend and backend technologies\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience with test automation tools and frameworks for UI, API, and integration testing\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eUnderstanding of React, TypeScript, .NET (C#), Node.js, APIs, and AWS‑based systems from a testing perspective\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience working with CI/CD pipelines, GitHub workflows, and containerized environments\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eKnowledge of Agile development methodologies and experience working in cross‑functional product teams\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong analytical, organizational, problem‑solving, and communication skills\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAbility to work independently while collaborating effectively across teams and stakeholders\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience with commerce, payments, financing, order management, or customer journey platforms is considered an advantage\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAtleast 4 years of professional experience in Software Quality Assurance\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that a change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate‑neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTogether, we are creating, collaborating, and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility. We are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eIs this you?\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf you are interested in joining the Polestar crew, don’t wait to submit your application. We apply a continuous selection process and the job post will remain open until the position is filled.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAs we move through the Swedish summer holiday season, there may be a slight delay in our process. We look forward to getting back to you in August.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eSend us your resume along with a short note on what makes this role interesting to you. We read everything.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric, by the way…\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":7973296},"datePosted":"2026-06-25T16:18:46+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Assar Gabrielssons väg 9","addressLocality":"Göteborg","postalCode":"418 78","addressCountry":"SE","addressRegion":"Nordics \u0026 UK"}}]}},{"id":"b4bbb9b2-3f3c-4b90-8e5a-08fa8804eb93","title":"Public Relations \u0026 Events Manager","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/7831116-public-relations-events-manager","date_published":"2026-06-01T20:04:37+02:00","content_html":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAt Polestar we don't just drive innovation in our cars – our entire business model is different from our competitors. We’re looking for a creative, innovative, experienced, and hands-on professional to drive and elevate Polestars brand awareness, consideration and reputation across Canada.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/strong\u003eAs the Public Relations \u0026amp; Events Manager your primary focus will be on developing and executing proactive public relations and events strategies for Polestar’s products, technology and consumer facing narratives. In partnership with Communications \u0026amp; Marketing, you will take lead in managing media, journalists and influencer relationships, and execute PR campaigns which drive brand awareness engagement and consideration. You will also be directly responsible for creating and executing focused events in order to deliver brand and business results in alignment with market objectives.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThis role will require 20-40% travel throughout Canada and reports to the Head of Marketing, Canada.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat you’ll do\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· \u003c/span\u003eDeliver and execute PR campaigns which build and maintain positive key media relationships for the company\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· \u003c/span\u003eOversee product communications from launch through lifecycle management\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· \u003c/span\u003eSupport corporate financial communications, including quarterly and annual reporting, ensuring clear, consistent messaging aligned with business performance and strategy\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· \u003c/span\u003eA\u003cspan\u003ect as the main PR contact for inquiries, statements, press escalations.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Lead experiential activities and events both for the media and the general public including product launches, auto shows, demo drives, influencer and sponsorship events.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· \u003c/span\u003eDrive consumer facing communication efforts to increase brand awareness, consideration, reputation\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· \u003c/span\u003eManage Canadian PR agencies of record, Event agency(ies), as well as vendor partners, ensuring quality completion of deliverables in support of departmental goals\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Foster close collaboration with Communication \u0026amp; Marketing peers, supporting them as necessary\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· \u003c/span\u003eFor PR and Marketing needs, manage and oversee the fleet vehicles, asset inventory and logistics, ensuring optimal usage, availability and maintenance\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Track, monitor and report PR and event performance and KPIs, manage departmental budget\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Upkeep and maintain internal archives and asset library\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Support in ad hoc projects, events and tasks as needed\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWho you are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· 7 – 10 years of experience in Public Relations or Communications\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Bachelor’s degree in communications, Journalism or related field\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Proven experience managing events, influencer programs, and external partners.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Excellent communication skills – both written \u0026amp; verbal, and both in English and in French required\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Experience working for an automotive manufacturer, or a consumer PR Agency is highly desirable\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Proven track record of managing successful PR campaigns and engaging events\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Exceptional project management and multitasking abilities.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· You understand the basic technical intricacies of the automobile, or possess the desire and proficiency to learn them\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· You thrive working within a fast-paced, ever evolving work environment\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Comfortable managing budgets, timelines, and cross-functional projects.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that a change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate-neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative. Together, we are creating, collaborating and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs this you?\u003c/strong\u003e If you are interested in joining the Polestar family, don't wait with submitting your application. We apply a continuous selection process and the job post will be open until the position is filled.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric by the way...\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Public Relations \u0026 Events Manager","description":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAt Polestar we don't just drive innovation in our cars – our entire business model is different from our competitors. We’re looking for a creative, innovative, experienced, and hands-on professional to drive and elevate Polestars brand awareness, consideration and reputation across Canada.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/strong\u003eAs the Public Relations \u0026amp; Events Manager your primary focus will be on developing and executing proactive public relations and events strategies for Polestar’s products, technology and consumer facing narratives. In partnership with Communications \u0026amp; Marketing, you will take lead in managing media, journalists and influencer relationships, and execute PR campaigns which drive brand awareness engagement and consideration. You will also be directly responsible for creating and executing focused events in order to deliver brand and business results in alignment with market objectives.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThis role will require 20-40% travel throughout Canada and reports to the Head of Marketing, Canada.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat you’ll do\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· \u003c/span\u003eDeliver and execute PR campaigns which build and maintain positive key media relationships for the company\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· \u003c/span\u003eOversee product communications from launch through lifecycle management\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· \u003c/span\u003eSupport corporate financial communications, including quarterly and annual reporting, ensuring clear, consistent messaging aligned with business performance and strategy\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· \u003c/span\u003eA\u003cspan\u003ect as the main PR contact for inquiries, statements, press escalations.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Lead experiential activities and events both for the media and the general public including product launches, auto shows, demo drives, influencer and sponsorship events.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· \u003c/span\u003eDrive consumer facing communication efforts to increase brand awareness, consideration, reputation\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· \u003c/span\u003eManage Canadian PR agencies of record, Event agency(ies), as well as vendor partners, ensuring quality completion of deliverables in support of departmental goals\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Foster close collaboration with Communication \u0026amp; Marketing peers, supporting them as necessary\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· \u003c/span\u003eFor PR and Marketing needs, manage and oversee the fleet vehicles, asset inventory and logistics, ensuring optimal usage, availability and maintenance\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Track, monitor and report PR and event performance and KPIs, manage departmental budget\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Upkeep and maintain internal archives and asset library\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Support in ad hoc projects, events and tasks as needed\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWho you are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· 7 – 10 years of experience in Public Relations or Communications\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Bachelor’s degree in communications, Journalism or related field\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Proven experience managing events, influencer programs, and external partners.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Excellent communication skills – both written \u0026amp; verbal, and both in English and in French required\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Experience working for an automotive manufacturer, or a consumer PR Agency is highly desirable\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Proven track record of managing successful PR campaigns and engaging events\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Exceptional project management and multitasking abilities.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· You understand the basic technical intricacies of the automobile, or possess the desire and proficiency to learn them\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· You thrive working within a fast-paced, ever evolving work environment\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e· Comfortable managing budgets, timelines, and cross-functional projects.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that a change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate-neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative. Together, we are creating, collaborating and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs this you?\u003c/strong\u003e If you are interested in joining the Polestar family, don't wait with submitting your application. We apply a continuous selection process and the job post will be open until the position is filled.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric by the way...\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":7831116},"datePosted":"2026-06-01T20:04:37+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":null,"addressLocality":"Mascouche","postalCode":null,"addressCountry":"CA","addressRegion":"Canada"}}]}},{"id":"e0f2e7d4-1ad0-4a83-834c-c9590c10e367","title":"Space Specialist (Nantes)","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/7731796-space-specialist-nantes","date_published":"2026-05-13T13:45:26+02:00","content_html":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eRejoignez l’aventure POLESTAR avec le Groupe SOFILIO, acteur familial de référence en Pays de la Loire, et participez à l’émergence d’une nouvelle vision de la mobilité.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDans le cadre de son développement, le Groupe SOFILIO intègre aujourd’hui POLESTAR, marque innovante et engagée, dédiée à une mobilité électrique performante, design et responsable.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDécrivons le défi que nous proposons\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cspan\u003eNée en Suède, POLESTAR réinvente la mobilité électrique en alliant design épuré, innovation technologique et engagement environnemental.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLa marque incarne une approche avant-gardiste de l’automobile :\u003cbr\u003eperformance, durabilité et esthétique scandinave.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eNotre ambition? accélérer la transition vers une mobilité alliant puissance, élégance et conscience écologique.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eVos missions\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePlus qu’un(e) conseiller(e) commercial(e), vous incarnez l’expérience POLESTAR sur votre territoire (Pays de la Loire).\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eVous accompagnez chaque client dans une démarche immersive, moderne et personnalisée.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAccueillir, écouter et conseiller les clients dans un environnement premium et épuré\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFaire vivre une véritable expérience de marque : découverte des véhicules, essais, configuration digitale\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAccompagner le client à chaque étape, de la première rencontre jusqu’à la livraison\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDévelopper une relation durable et qualitative avec votre portefeuille clients\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eParticiper activement au lancement et au développement de POLESTAR sur votre secteur\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePromouvoir les services associés : financement, assurance, reprise, accessoires, entretien\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eQui vous êtes\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eNous recherchons un(e) professionnel(le) de la vente capable d’allier excellence relationnelle, sens du conseil et appétence pour l’innovation.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cspan\u003eVotre savoir-faire\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExpérience réussie dans la vente automobile (idéalement premium, électrique ou innovante)\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMaîtrise des techniques de vente et de la relation client haut de gamme\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSensibilité aux nouvelles technologies et à la mobilité électrique\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAisance avec les outils digitaux\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eVotre savoir-être\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExcellente présentation et sens du service\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eÉcoute, curiosité et capacité à inspirer confiance\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDynamisme, sourire et énergie positive\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eGoût du challenge et culture du résultat\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eEsprit pionnier et envie de participer à une aventure de lancement\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eC'est vous?\u003c/strong\u003e Si vous souhaitez rejoindre l'équipe Polestar, n'hésitez pas à postuler dès maintenant. Nous menons un processus de sélection en continu et l'offre d'emploi restera ouverte jusqu'à ce que le poste soit pourvu.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eÊtes-vous prêt pour l'aventure ? Une aventure 100 % électrique, d'ailleurs...\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Space Specialist (Nantes)","description":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eRejoignez l’aventure POLESTAR avec le Groupe SOFILIO, acteur familial de référence en Pays de la Loire, et participez à l’émergence d’une nouvelle vision de la mobilité.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDans le cadre de son développement, le Groupe SOFILIO intègre aujourd’hui POLESTAR, marque innovante et engagée, dédiée à une mobilité électrique performante, design et responsable.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDécrivons le défi que nous proposons\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cspan\u003eNée en Suède, POLESTAR réinvente la mobilité électrique en alliant design épuré, innovation technologique et engagement environnemental.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLa marque incarne une approche avant-gardiste de l’automobile :\u003cbr\u003eperformance, durabilité et esthétique scandinave.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eNotre ambition? accélérer la transition vers une mobilité alliant puissance, élégance et conscience écologique.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eVos missions\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePlus qu’un(e) conseiller(e) commercial(e), vous incarnez l’expérience POLESTAR sur votre territoire (Pays de la Loire).\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eVous accompagnez chaque client dans une démarche immersive, moderne et personnalisée.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAccueillir, écouter et conseiller les clients dans un environnement premium et épuré\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFaire vivre une véritable expérience de marque : découverte des véhicules, essais, configuration digitale\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAccompagner le client à chaque étape, de la première rencontre jusqu’à la livraison\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDévelopper une relation durable et qualitative avec votre portefeuille clients\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eParticiper activement au lancement et au développement de POLESTAR sur votre secteur\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePromouvoir les services associés : financement, assurance, reprise, accessoires, entretien\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eQui vous êtes\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eNous recherchons un(e) professionnel(le) de la vente capable d’allier excellence relationnelle, sens du conseil et appétence pour l’innovation.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cspan\u003eVotre savoir-faire\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExpérience réussie dans la vente automobile (idéalement premium, électrique ou innovante)\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMaîtrise des techniques de vente et de la relation client haut de gamme\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eSensibilité aux nouvelles technologies et à la mobilité électrique\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAisance avec les outils digitaux\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eVotre savoir-être\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eExcellente présentation et sens du service\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eÉcoute, curiosité et capacité à inspirer confiance\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDynamisme, sourire et énergie positive\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eGoût du challenge et culture du résultat\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eEsprit pionnier et envie de participer à une aventure de lancement\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eC'est vous?\u003c/strong\u003e Si vous souhaitez rejoindre l'équipe Polestar, n'hésitez pas à postuler dès maintenant. Nous menons un processus de sélection en continu et l'offre d'emploi restera ouverte jusqu'à ce que le poste soit pourvu.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eÊtes-vous prêt pour l'aventure ? Une aventure 100 % électrique, d'ailleurs...\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":7731796},"datePosted":"2026-05-13T13:45:26+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":null,"addressLocality":"Nantes","postalCode":null,"addressCountry":"FR","addressRegion":"EMEA"}}]}},{"id":"df3763ed-b75d-48a0-9b28-f68176d36769","title":"Customer Experience Advisor","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/7230514-customer-experience-advisor","date_published":"2026-02-13T21:16:24+01:00","content_html":"\u003cp\u003eAt Polestar, we don't just drive innovation in our cars – our entire business model is different from our competitors. We’re looking for a creative, innovative, experienced, and hands-on professional to be the primary point of contact with our customers and be the ambassador of Polestars premium brand experience.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAbout Polestar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is an electric performance car brand, determined to improve the society we live in by driving the change to sustainable mobility. We are a global team of highly talented individuals who share a passion to change the world. We challenge conventions and we challenge ourselves for the purpose of innovation. We believe innovation is a team effort and that just like each component is critical to the performance of our cars, each person working at Polestar is as important to the team and its performance. We work in close collaboration across empowered global teams that don’t settle for anything less than excellence. \u003cbr\u003e  \u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs this you?\u003c/strong\u003e If you are interested in joining the Polestar team, don't wait to submit your application. We apply a continuous selection process, and the job post will be open until the position is filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Customer Experience Advisor will be an important piece to the puzzle at Polestar and take ownership of the customer journey and resolution of customer inquiries. This person will be responsible for providing our customers with support through various channels including phone, email and chat. As a Customer Experience Advisor, you will play a pivotal role in delivering exceptional, personalized experiences to our customers, ensuring their journey with Polestar is seamless, delightful, and data driven. Your expertise in customer engagement, coupled with your passion for utilizing data to inform decisions, will help shape how we interact with and support our valued customers.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWe are hiring enthusiastic individuals for a number of shifts based in our Mascouche, Quebec HQ office. \u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhat you’ll do\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eProvide exceptional customer support across all touchpoints (live chat, email and phone) by addressing inquiries, resolving issues, and offering tailored solutions to meet customer needs.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAddress customer inquiries, concerns, and issues promptly, ensuring resolutions are effective and aligned with Polestar’s standards of service.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAct as the customer advocate, ensuring all customer interactions reflect Polestar’s commitment to quality and innovation, while maintaining a positive, empathetic, and personalized approach.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEngage with customers proactively, offering assistance, guidance, and relevant information to enhance their experience with Polestar before, during, and after their purchase.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eLeverage customer data and insights to identify trends, predict needs, and drive improvements in the customer experience. Ensure that feedback loops inform continuous enhancement of the Polestar experience.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eWork closely with the product, marketing, quality and operations teams to communicate customer feedback, ensure alignment on customer needs, and contribute to the ongoing refinement of Polestar’s offerings.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eUse customer feedback, data analytics, and performance metrics to identify opportunities for process optimization and enhancement of the overall customer journey.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePromote Polestar's values, products, and services, ensuring that every customer interaction reflects the brand’s standards of excellence and sustainability.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWho you are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMinimum of 2-3 years of experience in a customer-facing role, preferably in a high-end retail, automotive, or technology call center setting.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eProficient spoken and written communication in French-Canadian and English.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDemonstrated ability to deliver superior customer experiences by understanding customer needs and tailoring solutions to meet those needs.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience using Salesforce is preferred.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong verbal and written communication skills with an ability to connect with customers and colleagues effectively.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAbility to assess complex situations and offer creative, thoughtful solutions that prioritize the customer’s satisfaction and experience.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eComfortable working in a fast-paced environment where flexibility and innovation are essential to success.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eA strong interest in sustainable products and technologies, with a particular enthusiasm for electric vehicles and the Polestar brand.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that a change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate-neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative. Together, we are creating, collaborating and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs this you?\u003c/strong\u003e If you are interested in joining the Polestar family, don't wait with submitting your application. We apply a continuous selection process and the job post will be open until the position is filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric by the way...\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Customer Experience Advisor","description":"\u003cp\u003eAt Polestar, we don't just drive innovation in our cars – our entire business model is different from our competitors. We’re looking for a creative, innovative, experienced, and hands-on professional to be the primary point of contact with our customers and be the ambassador of Polestars premium brand experience.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAbout Polestar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is an electric performance car brand, determined to improve the society we live in by driving the change to sustainable mobility. We are a global team of highly talented individuals who share a passion to change the world. We challenge conventions and we challenge ourselves for the purpose of innovation. We believe innovation is a team effort and that just like each component is critical to the performance of our cars, each person working at Polestar is as important to the team and its performance. We work in close collaboration across empowered global teams that don’t settle for anything less than excellence. \u003cbr\u003e  \u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs this you?\u003c/strong\u003e If you are interested in joining the Polestar team, don't wait to submit your application. We apply a continuous selection process, and the job post will be open until the position is filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Customer Experience Advisor will be an important piece to the puzzle at Polestar and take ownership of the customer journey and resolution of customer inquiries. This person will be responsible for providing our customers with support through various channels including phone, email and chat. As a Customer Experience Advisor, you will play a pivotal role in delivering exceptional, personalized experiences to our customers, ensuring their journey with Polestar is seamless, delightful, and data driven. Your expertise in customer engagement, coupled with your passion for utilizing data to inform decisions, will help shape how we interact with and support our valued customers.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWe are hiring enthusiastic individuals for a number of shifts based in our Mascouche, Quebec HQ office. \u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhat you’ll do\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eProvide exceptional customer support across all touchpoints (live chat, email and phone) by addressing inquiries, resolving issues, and offering tailored solutions to meet customer needs.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAddress customer inquiries, concerns, and issues promptly, ensuring resolutions are effective and aligned with Polestar’s standards of service.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAct as the customer advocate, ensuring all customer interactions reflect Polestar’s commitment to quality and innovation, while maintaining a positive, empathetic, and personalized approach.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEngage with customers proactively, offering assistance, guidance, and relevant information to enhance their experience with Polestar before, during, and after their purchase.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eLeverage customer data and insights to identify trends, predict needs, and drive improvements in the customer experience. Ensure that feedback loops inform continuous enhancement of the Polestar experience.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eWork closely with the product, marketing, quality and operations teams to communicate customer feedback, ensure alignment on customer needs, and contribute to the ongoing refinement of Polestar’s offerings.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eUse customer feedback, data analytics, and performance metrics to identify opportunities for process optimization and enhancement of the overall customer journey.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePromote Polestar's values, products, and services, ensuring that every customer interaction reflects the brand’s standards of excellence and sustainability.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWho you are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMinimum of 2-3 years of experience in a customer-facing role, preferably in a high-end retail, automotive, or technology call center setting.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eProficient spoken and written communication in French-Canadian and English.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDemonstrated ability to deliver superior customer experiences by understanding customer needs and tailoring solutions to meet those needs.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExperience using Salesforce is preferred.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStrong verbal and written communication skills with an ability to connect with customers and colleagues effectively.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAbility to assess complex situations and offer creative, thoughtful solutions that prioritize the customer’s satisfaction and experience.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eComfortable working in a fast-paced environment where flexibility and innovation are essential to success.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eA strong interest in sustainable products and technologies, with a particular enthusiasm for electric vehicles and the Polestar brand.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that a change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate-neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative. Together, we are creating, collaborating and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs this you?\u003c/strong\u003e If you are interested in joining the Polestar family, don't wait with submitting your application. We apply a continuous selection process and the job post will be open until the position is filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric by the way...\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":7230514},"datePosted":"2026-02-13T21:16:24+01:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":null,"addressLocality":"Mascouche","postalCode":null,"addressCountry":"CA","addressRegion":"Canada"}}]}},{"id":"28b38d11-9ac0-4d61-8d1a-4871eae46039","title":"Customer Experience Advisor","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/7189608-customer-experience-advisor","date_published":"2026-02-06T21:11:48+01:00","content_html":"\u003cp\u003eAt Polestar, we don't just drive innovation in our cars – our entire business model is different from our competitors. We’re looking for a creative, innovative, experienced, and hands-on professional to be the primary point of contact with our customers and be the ambassador of Polestars premium brand experience.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAbout Polestar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is an electric performance car brand, determined to improve the society we live in by driving the change to sustainable mobility. We are a global team of highly talented individuals who share a passion to change the world. We challenge conventions and we challenge ourselves for the purpose of innovation. We believe innovation is a team effort and that just like each component is critical to the performance of our cars, each person working at Polestar is as important to the team and its performance. We work in close collaboration across empowered global teams that don’t settle for anything less than excellence. \u003cbr\u003e  \u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs this you?\u003c/strong\u003e If you are interested in joining the Polestar family, don't wait to submit your application. We apply a continuous selection process, and the job post will be open until the position is filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eThis is a contract position with potential for extension or conversion to full-time.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Customer Experience Advisor will be an important piece to the puzzle at Polestar and take ownership of the customer journey and resolution of customer inquiries. This person will be responsible for providing our customers with support through various channels including phone, email and chat.\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhat you’ll do\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eBrand advocate and consumer-centric individual who will strive to provide best-in-class experiences for our consumers.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eWork cross-functionally with peers and upper management to solve complex escalations and enhance the customer journey\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eManage inbound communications for product, service, leads and support requests\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eReceive and respond to customer communications, cases, or chats through to resolution\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eWork with Polestar Spaces \u0026amp; Service Points to ensure seamless communication for all involved parties\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eFollow up with current customer product, service, and support inquiries\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eBuild and maintain professional relationships with our customers throughout their experience\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eResolve and handle incoming customer advocacy cases through to resolution escalating to the appropriate team member where necessary\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDeliver a white glove customer experience through all available methods of communication\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStay up to date on Polestar news, product and software\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWho you are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAssociate degree or higher\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePrevious experience in call center environment, automotive, luxury retail or sales is highly desirable\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eFluency in English required, Bilingual is a plus!\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou have a passion for customer experience and being the ambassador of a brand\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eTech savvy with knowledge of call center and telephony systems. Salesforce experience a plus.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou have excellent verbal and written communication skills \u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou are an agile learner and comfortable with technology, learning new tools, and able to work with a variety of content areas/teams. \u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eProven project management skills, stakeholder management, time management, and prioritization when managing multiple projects. \u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou have attention to the details, and thrive in an ever-evolving work atmosphere \u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that a change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate-neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative. Together, we are creating, collaborating and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs this you?\u003c/strong\u003e If you are interested in joining the Polestar family, don't wait with submitting your application. We apply a continuous selection process and the job post will be open until the position is filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric by the way...\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Customer Experience Advisor","description":"\u003cp\u003eAt Polestar, we don't just drive innovation in our cars – our entire business model is different from our competitors. We’re looking for a creative, innovative, experienced, and hands-on professional to be the primary point of contact with our customers and be the ambassador of Polestars premium brand experience.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAbout Polestar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is an electric performance car brand, determined to improve the society we live in by driving the change to sustainable mobility. We are a global team of highly talented individuals who share a passion to change the world. We challenge conventions and we challenge ourselves for the purpose of innovation. We believe innovation is a team effort and that just like each component is critical to the performance of our cars, each person working at Polestar is as important to the team and its performance. We work in close collaboration across empowered global teams that don’t settle for anything less than excellence. \u003cbr\u003e  \u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs this you?\u003c/strong\u003e If you are interested in joining the Polestar family, don't wait to submit your application. We apply a continuous selection process, and the job post will be open until the position is filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eThis is a contract position with potential for extension or conversion to full-time.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLet us describe the challenge we offer\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Customer Experience Advisor will be an important piece to the puzzle at Polestar and take ownership of the customer journey and resolution of customer inquiries. This person will be responsible for providing our customers with support through various channels including phone, email and chat.\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhat you’ll do\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eBrand advocate and consumer-centric individual who will strive to provide best-in-class experiences for our consumers.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eWork cross-functionally with peers and upper management to solve complex escalations and enhance the customer journey\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eManage inbound communications for product, service, leads and support requests\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eReceive and respond to customer communications, cases, or chats through to resolution\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eWork with Polestar Spaces \u0026amp; Service Points to ensure seamless communication for all involved parties\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eFollow up with current customer product, service, and support inquiries\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eBuild and maintain professional relationships with our customers throughout their experience\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eResolve and handle incoming customer advocacy cases through to resolution escalating to the appropriate team member where necessary\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDeliver a white glove customer experience through all available methods of communication\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStay up to date on Polestar news, product and software\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWho you are\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAssociate degree or higher\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePrevious experience in call center environment, automotive, luxury retail or sales is highly desirable\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eFluency in English required, Bilingual is a plus!\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou have a passion for customer experience and being the ambassador of a brand\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eTech savvy with knowledge of call center and telephony systems. Salesforce experience a plus.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou have excellent verbal and written communication skills \u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou are an agile learner and comfortable with technology, learning new tools, and able to work with a variety of content areas/teams. \u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eProven project management skills, stakeholder management, time management, and prioritization when managing multiple projects. \u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou have attention to the details, and thrive in an ever-evolving work atmosphere \u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePeople at Polestar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe know that a change is needed. We also know that each one of us can help bring about that change. Our commitment to becoming climate-neutral by 2040 is just as important to us as being inclusive, diverse, and innovative. Together, we are creating, collaborating and experimenting to usher in a new era of sustainable mobility.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe are an electric performance brand, determined to improve the society we live in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs this you?\u003c/strong\u003e If you are interested in joining the Polestar family, don't wait with submitting your application. We apply a continuous selection process and the job post will be open until the position is filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre you ready for the journey? Which is electric by the way...\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":7189608},"datePosted":"2026-02-06T21:11:48+01:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"777 MacArthur Blvd","addressLocality":"Mahwah","postalCode":"07430","addressCountry":"US","addressRegion":"North America"}}]}},{"id":"20c20472-de15-4bb3-b2b3-d5ccef26beca","title":"Customer Engagement Advisor","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/6595224-customer-engagement-advisor","date_published":"2025-10-10T15:35:51+02:00","content_html":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe're currently looking for a Customer Engagement Advisor. Someone to join our Customer Experience team and play a key role in putting our customers first, and ensuring our Customer Engagement Centre are offering finest levels of customer service. Someone with a passion for electric mobility, an interest in technology, and a desire to create the change we know is needed.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWorking directly with the Contact Centre Team Leaders, our Contact Centre Manager and our Customer Engagement Centre team this role will be key in delivering a hassle-free experience for all our customers.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis position is located at our Bicester office and will require a minimum of three days in our office. We believe in a hybrid model when it comes to remote and onsite work, knowing that both in-person collaboration and individual time to focus are needed. What matters most is that people get the time and support to do what needs to be done. And to enjoy doing it, of course.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe responsibilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn this role, you'll be expected to champion all areas of customer engagement, putting the customer first in everything you do. Working as a member of the Customer Engagement department, you'll be instrumental in our ambition to be the best in class for customer service and offer all Polestar customers the finest experience. See below for a more thorough breakdown of the various tasks and areas you'll be responsible for:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eHandle enquiries from customers via Inbound Calls, Emails, Cases and chats\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eOutbound follow up and delivery support calls\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eBecome a champion of the Polestar products to be able to give customers the best advice and support\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eFirst line Complaint resolution\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eOther tasks as required for the role\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe ideal candidate\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn order to succeed in this role, and at Polestar in general, there are a few characteristics you'll need to have. Integrity, Kindness and Commitment. The ability to take the initiative, to meet set deadlines and requirements, and to always think customer first.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs a person you have great time management, and like to work in a team environment. You are also a digital-minded, flexible and agile individual who thrives working in fast-paced and dynamic environment and who has a can-do attitude and a self-starter approach. You are able to handle a broad portfolio of tasks and are confident supporting customers directly on a one to one basis.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn addition, you'll need the following:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAt least 6 months of experience in front line Customer Service roles\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePrevious complaints or escalations experience\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExcellent oral and written communication in English\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAble to work shifts across 8am to 6pm Monday to Friday. (Overtime may be available)\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eKnowledge of Salesforce is a benefit\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eGood knowledge of Excel \u0026amp; PowerPoint\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is an international company, with various backgrounds represented. English, therefore, is the language of written and spoken communication. And though we have a global presence, we maintain the growth-mindset. Change happens often at Polestar. But so does progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf the above matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. Our selection process is ongoing, and the job advert will remain open until it’s filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e#LI-AH1\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Customer Engagement Advisor","description":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe opportunity\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe're currently looking for a Customer Engagement Advisor. Someone to join our Customer Experience team and play a key role in putting our customers first, and ensuring our Customer Engagement Centre are offering finest levels of customer service. Someone with a passion for electric mobility, an interest in technology, and a desire to create the change we know is needed.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWorking directly with the Contact Centre Team Leaders, our Contact Centre Manager and our Customer Engagement Centre team this role will be key in delivering a hassle-free experience for all our customers.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis position is located at our Bicester office and will require a minimum of three days in our office. We believe in a hybrid model when it comes to remote and onsite work, knowing that both in-person collaboration and individual time to focus are needed. What matters most is that people get the time and support to do what needs to be done. And to enjoy doing it, of course.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe responsibilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn this role, you'll be expected to champion all areas of customer engagement, putting the customer first in everything you do. Working as a member of the Customer Engagement department, you'll be instrumental in our ambition to be the best in class for customer service and offer all Polestar customers the finest experience. See below for a more thorough breakdown of the various tasks and areas you'll be responsible for:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eHandle enquiries from customers via Inbound Calls, Emails, Cases and chats\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eOutbound follow up and delivery support calls\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eBecome a champion of the Polestar products to be able to give customers the best advice and support\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eFirst line Complaint resolution\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eOther tasks as required for the role\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe ideal candidate\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn order to succeed in this role, and at Polestar in general, there are a few characteristics you'll need to have. Integrity, Kindness and Commitment. The ability to take the initiative, to meet set deadlines and requirements, and to always think customer first.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs a person you have great time management, and like to work in a team environment. You are also a digital-minded, flexible and agile individual who thrives working in fast-paced and dynamic environment and who has a can-do attitude and a self-starter approach. You are able to handle a broad portfolio of tasks and are confident supporting customers directly on a one to one basis.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn addition, you'll need the following:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAt least 6 months of experience in front line Customer Service roles\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePrevious complaints or escalations experience\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExcellent oral and written communication in English\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAble to work shifts across 8am to 6pm Monday to Friday. (Overtime may be available)\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eKnowledge of Salesforce is a benefit\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eGood knowledge of Excel \u0026amp; PowerPoint\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar is an international company, with various backgrounds represented. English, therefore, is the language of written and spoken communication. And though we have a global presence, we maintain the growth-mindset. Change happens often at Polestar. But so does progress. Expect an accelerating, exciting environment.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe process\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf the above matches your ambitions, be sure to apply. Our selection process is ongoing, and the job advert will remain open until it’s filled.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e#LI-AH1\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":6595224},"datePosted":"2025-10-10T15:35:51+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"OX27 8FY","addressLocality":"Bicester","postalCode":"OX27 8FY","addressCountry":"GB","addressRegion":"Nordics \u0026 UK"}}]}},{"id":"794d5ee8-f6ec-4cff-9377-ecd358ea5b00","title":"Rechtsreferendar (m/w/d)  | Legal Commercial","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/6468430-rechtsreferendar-m-w-d-legal-commercial","date_published":"2025-09-18T08:36:23+02:00","content_html":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDie Chance\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWir suchen derzeit einen Rechtsreferendar (m/w/d) in der Wahlstation. Du wirst Teil unseres Commercial Legal Teams und unterstützt bei der Vertragsgestaltung, rechtlichen Beratung sowie bei Projekten rund um unsere nationalen und internationalen Geschäftsaktivitäten.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDu hast Leidenschaft für Elektromobilität, Interesse an Technologie und den Wunsch, den Wandel in der Automobilindustrie aktiv mitzugestalten. \u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn unserem Commercial Legal Team bearbeitest du die gesamte Bandbreite des Wirtschafts- und Vertragsrechts und bekommst einen einmaligen Einblick in die Tätigkeit einer international agierenden Rechtsabteilung. Du kannst Deine juristische Expertise mit unternehmerischem Denken verbinden und unterstützt so das Business mit pragmatischen und praxisorientierten Rat.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDiese Position ist an unserem Standort in Köln, Deutschland\u003cstrong\u003e, \u003c/strong\u003eangesiedelt, mit der Möglichkeit hybriden Arbeitens. Wir glauben an ein Modell, das sowohl Präsenz als auch Remote-Arbeit verbindet, denn Zusammenarbeit vor Ort ist genauso wichtig wie konzentriertes Arbeiten im eigenen Rhythmus. Wichtig ist für uns vor allem, dass Du die Unterstützung bekommst, die Du brauchst, um Deine Aufgaben erfolgreich und mit Freude zu erledigen.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDeine Aufgaben\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn dieser Rolle wird von Dir erwartet, die abteilungsübergreifendenden Stakeholder bei allen Fragestellungen im Bereich Commercial zu unterstützen. Als Mitglied des Commercial Legal Teams bist du maßgeblich für die Sicherstellung einer praxisnahen und lösungsorientierten Rechtsberatung für das Tagesgeschäft sowie für strategische Projekte. Konkret bedeutet das:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eErstellung, Prüfung und Gestaltung von Verträgen in allen Bereichen des Tagesgeschäfts, insbesondere in Bezug auf die Vertriebskanäle \u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUnterstützung bei strategischen Projekten\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eErstellung von Recherchen und rechtlichen Einschätzungen im lokalen und internationalen Kontext \u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eZusammenarbeit mit dem internationalen Legal-Team von Polestar\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDein Profil\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eUm in dieser Rolle erfolgreich zu sein, und bei Polestar generell, bringst du Eigenschaften wie Neugier, Flexibilität und Eigeninitiative mit. Du kannst Prioritäten setzen, Fristen einhalten und weißt, wann es besser ist, Ideen loszulassen, um pragmatische Lösungen zu finden. Außerdem bist du kommunikationsstark, kannst eigenverantwortlich arbeiten, hast eine schnelle Auffassungsgabe und arbeitest gerne im internationalen Umfeld.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDarüber hinaus bringst du folgende Qualifikationen mit:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eÜberdurchschnittlichem Ergebnis im Ersten Staatsexamen\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVorkenntnisse am Handels-, Vertrags- und Kartellrecht, idealerweise erworben durch erste Praxiserfahrungen \u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSicherer Umgang mit MS Office und Affinität zu digitalen Tools\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar ist ein internationales Unternehmen mit vielfältigen Hintergründen. Englisch ist daher unsere gemeinsame Sprache in Wort und Schrift. Auch wenn wir global agieren, bewahren wir unsere Wachstums-Mentalität.  Veränderung gehört bei Polestar zum Alltag - ebenso wie Fortschritt. Dich erwartet ein dynamisches, spannendes Umfeld.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDer Bewerbungsprozess \u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWenn das nach Deiner nächsten Herausforderung klingt, bewirb Dich jetzt. Unser Auswahlprozess läuft fortlaufend, und die Ausschreibung bleibt offen, bis die Stelle besetzt ist. \u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDie Reise mit Polestar ist elektrisch.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Rechtsreferendar (m/w/d)  | Legal Commercial","description":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDie Chance\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWir suchen derzeit einen Rechtsreferendar (m/w/d) in der Wahlstation. Du wirst Teil unseres Commercial Legal Teams und unterstützt bei der Vertragsgestaltung, rechtlichen Beratung sowie bei Projekten rund um unsere nationalen und internationalen Geschäftsaktivitäten.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDu hast Leidenschaft für Elektromobilität, Interesse an Technologie und den Wunsch, den Wandel in der Automobilindustrie aktiv mitzugestalten. \u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn unserem Commercial Legal Team bearbeitest du die gesamte Bandbreite des Wirtschafts- und Vertragsrechts und bekommst einen einmaligen Einblick in die Tätigkeit einer international agierenden Rechtsabteilung. Du kannst Deine juristische Expertise mit unternehmerischem Denken verbinden und unterstützt so das Business mit pragmatischen und praxisorientierten Rat.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDiese Position ist an unserem Standort in Köln, Deutschland\u003cstrong\u003e, \u003c/strong\u003eangesiedelt, mit der Möglichkeit hybriden Arbeitens. Wir glauben an ein Modell, das sowohl Präsenz als auch Remote-Arbeit verbindet, denn Zusammenarbeit vor Ort ist genauso wichtig wie konzentriertes Arbeiten im eigenen Rhythmus. Wichtig ist für uns vor allem, dass Du die Unterstützung bekommst, die Du brauchst, um Deine Aufgaben erfolgreich und mit Freude zu erledigen.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDeine Aufgaben\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn dieser Rolle wird von Dir erwartet, die abteilungsübergreifendenden Stakeholder bei allen Fragestellungen im Bereich Commercial zu unterstützen. Als Mitglied des Commercial Legal Teams bist du maßgeblich für die Sicherstellung einer praxisnahen und lösungsorientierten Rechtsberatung für das Tagesgeschäft sowie für strategische Projekte. Konkret bedeutet das:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eErstellung, Prüfung und Gestaltung von Verträgen in allen Bereichen des Tagesgeschäfts, insbesondere in Bezug auf die Vertriebskanäle \u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUnterstützung bei strategischen Projekten\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eErstellung von Recherchen und rechtlichen Einschätzungen im lokalen und internationalen Kontext \u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eZusammenarbeit mit dem internationalen Legal-Team von Polestar\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDein Profil\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eUm in dieser Rolle erfolgreich zu sein, und bei Polestar generell, bringst du Eigenschaften wie Neugier, Flexibilität und Eigeninitiative mit. Du kannst Prioritäten setzen, Fristen einhalten und weißt, wann es besser ist, Ideen loszulassen, um pragmatische Lösungen zu finden. Außerdem bist du kommunikationsstark, kannst eigenverantwortlich arbeiten, hast eine schnelle Auffassungsgabe und arbeitest gerne im internationalen Umfeld.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDarüber hinaus bringst du folgende Qualifikationen mit:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eÜberdurchschnittlichem Ergebnis im Ersten Staatsexamen\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVorkenntnisse am Handels-, Vertrags- und Kartellrecht, idealerweise erworben durch erste Praxiserfahrungen \u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSicherer Umgang mit MS Office und Affinität zu digitalen Tools\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar ist ein internationales Unternehmen mit vielfältigen Hintergründen. Englisch ist daher unsere gemeinsame Sprache in Wort und Schrift. Auch wenn wir global agieren, bewahren wir unsere Wachstums-Mentalität.  Veränderung gehört bei Polestar zum Alltag - ebenso wie Fortschritt. Dich erwartet ein dynamisches, spannendes Umfeld.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDer Bewerbungsprozess \u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWenn das nach Deiner nächsten Herausforderung klingt, bewirb Dich jetzt. Unser Auswahlprozess läuft fortlaufend, und die Ausschreibung bleibt offen, bis die Stelle besetzt ist. \u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDie Reise mit Polestar ist elektrisch.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":6468430},"datePosted":"2025-09-18T08:36:23+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":null,"addressLocality":"Cologne","postalCode":"50667","addressCountry":"DE","addressRegion":"Central Europe"}}]}},{"id":"73238f8e-02f4-4f34-a0d4-acbde4987ca0","title":"Customer Engagement Advisor | Teilzeit","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/5156883-customer-engagement-advisor-teilzeit","date_published":"2024-11-04T09:40:12+01:00","content_html":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDie Möglichkeit\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWir sind auf der Suche nach einem Customer Engagement Advisor, der in unserem Customer Engagement Center nachhaltige Beziehungen zu unseren KundInnen aufbaut. Du solltest dich für Elektromobilität und neue Technologien begeistern und den Wunsch haben, die notwendigen Veränderungen herbeizuführen, um das Unternehmen Polestar weiter zu stärken.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDer Arbeitsplatz befindet sich in unserem Büro in Köln oder Wien. Wir glauben an ein hybrides Modell, wenn es um Remote- und Arbeit vor Ort geht, da wir wissen, dass sowohl persönliche Zusammenarbeit als auch individuelle Zeit notwendig sind, um effizient zu arbeiten.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDie Verantwortung\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAls Teil unseres Customer Engagement Teams arbeitest du direkt mit Kunden sowie mit unseren Partnern zusammen, um gemeinsam hervorragende Kundenerlebnisse zu schaffen. Als Customer Engagement Advisor spielst du eine Schlüsselrolle bei der Betreuung von Interessenten und Kunden während der gesamten Customer Journey.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eZu deinen Aufgaben gehören folgende Tätigkeiten:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eKommunikation per Telefon, Chat und E-Mail sowie Bearbeitung von Informationsanfragen über die Website. Wir haben eine Mischung aus Inbound- und Outbound-Kommunikation, mit dem Schwerpunkt auf Kundenservice und Unterstützung im Bestellprozess.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eBeratung \u003cspan\u003eund Begleitung potenzieller Kunden durch den Online-Bestellprozess ihres Polestar.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eProblemlösung für potenzielle und bestehende Kunden.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eUm unseren Kunden ein reibungsloses Erlebnis zu bieten, wirst du eng mit internen Teams und Abteilungen zusammenarbeiten.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWährend deiner ersten Wochen bei Polestar lernst Du dein Team, die Rolle und den „Polestar Way“ kennen. Danach knüpfen wir mit einem Trainings- und Development-Programm an, das dir fortlaufend neue Möglichkeiten zum Lernen und der Erweiterung deiner Fähigkeiten bietet – wir leben eine positive und wertschätzende Coaching- und Feedbackkultur für alle Polestar-MitarbeiterInnen.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDer ideale Kandidat\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWir suchen jemanden, der immer ein offenes Ohr für unsere KundInnen hat und motiviert ist, einen erstklassigen Service zu bieten. Dabei geben wir dir alle Werkzeuge an die Hand, die Du brauchst, um in deiner Rolle als Customer Engagement Advisor erfolgreich zu sein.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDer beste Hinweis darauf, ob dir dieser Job gefallen wird? Du zeichnest dich durch hervorragende Kommunikationsfähigkeiten aus, indem du in der Lage bist die Fragen unserer KundInnen auf den Punkt zu beantworten. Du bist wortgewandt und kannst unseren KundInnen unser Markenerlebnis näher bringen. Du verfügst über eine flexible und praktische Einstellung, um Lösungen zu finden und bleibst dank deines guten Zeitmanagements auch in hektischen Situationen ruhig. In unserer Arbeitsweise, in der wir Wert auf Selbstorganisation legen, sind Kooperation und Kommunikation wesentliche Fähigkeiten.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDarüber hinaus bringst du folgende Qualifikationen mit:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eKaufmännische oder technische Berufsausbildung oder Studium.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAusgezeichnete \u003cspan\u003eKommunikationsfähigkeiten (mündlich und schriftlich) in Deutsch und gute Kenntnisse der englischen Sprache. Französisch oder Italienisch sind ebenfalls willkommen aber kein Muss.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eErfahrung im Kundenservice oder Vertrieb mit Fokus auf Beantwortung von Anrufen, E-Mails, Tickets oder Erfahrungen im täglichen Kundenkontakt.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eGute Auffassungsgabe, um dich schnell in neue Systeme \u0026amp; Prozesse einarbeiten zu können.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eTeamorientierte Arbeitsweise.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIdealerweise erste Erfahrungen in der Automobilindustrie.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar ist ein internationales Unternehmen, in dem Menschen unterschiedlicher Herkunft zusammenarbeiten.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWir sind auf der ganzen Welt präsent und haben uns den Wachstumsgedanken bewahrt, weshalb Veränderungen bei Polestar an der Tagesordnung sind. Aber das gilt auch für den Fortschritt. Du kannst dich auf ein spannendes und aufregendes Umfeld freuen.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDer Prozess\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWenn die oben genannten Punkte auf dich zutreffen, solltest du dich unbedingt bewerben. Unser Auswahlverfahren ist noch nicht abgeschlossen und die Stelle wird so lange ausgeschrieben, bis sie besetzt ist.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Customer Engagement Advisor | Teilzeit","description":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDie Möglichkeit\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWir sind auf der Suche nach einem Customer Engagement Advisor, der in unserem Customer Engagement Center nachhaltige Beziehungen zu unseren KundInnen aufbaut. Du solltest dich für Elektromobilität und neue Technologien begeistern und den Wunsch haben, die notwendigen Veränderungen herbeizuführen, um das Unternehmen Polestar weiter zu stärken.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDer Arbeitsplatz befindet sich in unserem Büro in Köln oder Wien. Wir glauben an ein hybrides Modell, wenn es um Remote- und Arbeit vor Ort geht, da wir wissen, dass sowohl persönliche Zusammenarbeit als auch individuelle Zeit notwendig sind, um effizient zu arbeiten.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDie Verantwortung\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAls Teil unseres Customer Engagement Teams arbeitest du direkt mit Kunden sowie mit unseren Partnern zusammen, um gemeinsam hervorragende Kundenerlebnisse zu schaffen. Als Customer Engagement Advisor spielst du eine Schlüsselrolle bei der Betreuung von Interessenten und Kunden während der gesamten Customer Journey.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eZu deinen Aufgaben gehören folgende Tätigkeiten:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eKommunikation per Telefon, Chat und E-Mail sowie Bearbeitung von Informationsanfragen über die Website. Wir haben eine Mischung aus Inbound- und Outbound-Kommunikation, mit dem Schwerpunkt auf Kundenservice und Unterstützung im Bestellprozess.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eBeratung \u003cspan\u003eund Begleitung potenzieller Kunden durch den Online-Bestellprozess ihres Polestar.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eProblemlösung für potenzielle und bestehende Kunden.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eUm unseren Kunden ein reibungsloses Erlebnis zu bieten, wirst du eng mit internen Teams und Abteilungen zusammenarbeiten.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWährend deiner ersten Wochen bei Polestar lernst Du dein Team, die Rolle und den „Polestar Way“ kennen. Danach knüpfen wir mit einem Trainings- und Development-Programm an, das dir fortlaufend neue Möglichkeiten zum Lernen und der Erweiterung deiner Fähigkeiten bietet – wir leben eine positive und wertschätzende Coaching- und Feedbackkultur für alle Polestar-MitarbeiterInnen.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDer ideale Kandidat\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWir suchen jemanden, der immer ein offenes Ohr für unsere KundInnen hat und motiviert ist, einen erstklassigen Service zu bieten. Dabei geben wir dir alle Werkzeuge an die Hand, die Du brauchst, um in deiner Rolle als Customer Engagement Advisor erfolgreich zu sein.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDer beste Hinweis darauf, ob dir dieser Job gefallen wird? Du zeichnest dich durch hervorragende Kommunikationsfähigkeiten aus, indem du in der Lage bist die Fragen unserer KundInnen auf den Punkt zu beantworten. Du bist wortgewandt und kannst unseren KundInnen unser Markenerlebnis näher bringen. Du verfügst über eine flexible und praktische Einstellung, um Lösungen zu finden und bleibst dank deines guten Zeitmanagements auch in hektischen Situationen ruhig. In unserer Arbeitsweise, in der wir Wert auf Selbstorganisation legen, sind Kooperation und Kommunikation wesentliche Fähigkeiten.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDarüber hinaus bringst du folgende Qualifikationen mit:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eKaufmännische oder technische Berufsausbildung oder Studium.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAusgezeichnete \u003cspan\u003eKommunikationsfähigkeiten (mündlich und schriftlich) in Deutsch und gute Kenntnisse der englischen Sprache. Französisch oder Italienisch sind ebenfalls willkommen aber kein Muss.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eErfahrung im Kundenservice oder Vertrieb mit Fokus auf Beantwortung von Anrufen, E-Mails, Tickets oder Erfahrungen im täglichen Kundenkontakt.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eGute Auffassungsgabe, um dich schnell in neue Systeme \u0026amp; Prozesse einarbeiten zu können.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eTeamorientierte Arbeitsweise.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIdealerweise erste Erfahrungen in der Automobilindustrie.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar ist ein internationales Unternehmen, in dem Menschen unterschiedlicher Herkunft zusammenarbeiten.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWir sind auf der ganzen Welt präsent und haben uns den Wachstumsgedanken bewahrt, weshalb Veränderungen bei Polestar an der Tagesordnung sind. Aber das gilt auch für den Fortschritt. Du kannst dich auf ein spannendes und aufregendes Umfeld freuen.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDer Prozess\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWenn die oben genannten Punkte auf dich zutreffen, solltest du dich unbedingt bewerben. Unser Auswahlverfahren ist noch nicht abgeschlossen und die Stelle wird so lange ausgeschrieben, bis sie besetzt ist.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":5156883},"datePosted":"2024-11-04T09:40:12+01:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"1150","addressLocality":"Vienna","postalCode":"1150","addressCountry":"AT","addressRegion":"Central Europe"}},{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":null,"addressLocality":"Cologne","postalCode":"50667","addressCountry":"DE","addressRegion":"Central Europe"}}]}},{"id":"77c2860b-daad-4197-ad84-b0589f78e209","title":"Werkstudent I Customer Engagement Advisor | Germany","url":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com/jobs/4800529-werkstudent-i-customer-engagement-advisor-germany","date_published":"2024-08-06T10:13:04+02:00","content_html":"\u003cp\u003eWerkstudent I Customer Engagement Advisor | Germany\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDie Möglichkeit\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWir suchen einen Werkstudenten (m/w) für 20 Stunden pro Woche, der in unserem Customer Engagement Center\u003cspan\u003e, der in unserem Customer Engagement Center nachhaltige Beziehungen zu unseren KundInnen aufbaut. Du solltest dich für Elektromobilität und neue Technologien begeistern und den Wunsch haben, die notwendigen Veränderungen herbeizuführen, um das Unternehmen Polestar weiter zu stärken.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDer Arbeitsplatz befindet sich in unserem Büro in Köln. Wir glauben an ein hybrides Modell, wenn es um Remote- und Arbeit vor Ort geht, da wir wissen, dass sowohl persönliche Zusammenarbeit als auch individuelle Zeit notwendig sind, um effizient zu arbeiten.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDie Verantwortung\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAls Teil unseres Customer Engagement Teams arbeitest du direkt mit Kunden sowie mit unseren Partnern zusammen, um gemeinsam hervorragende Kundenerlebnisse zu schaffen. Als Customer Engagement Advisor spielst du eine Schlüsselrolle bei der Betreuung von Interessenten und Kunden während der gesamten Customer Journey.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eZu deinen Aufgaben gehören folgende Tätigkeiten:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eKommunikation per Telefon, Chat und E-Mail sowie Bearbeitung von Informationsanfragen über die Website. Wir haben eine Mischung aus Inbound- und Outbound-Kommunikation, mit dem Schwerpunkt auf Kundenservice und Unterstützung im Bestellprozess.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eBeratung und Begleitung potenzieller Kunden durch den Online-Bestellprozess ihres Polestar.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eProblemlösung für potenzielle und bestehende Kunden.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eUm unseren Kunden ein reibungsloses Erlebnis zu bieten, wirst du eng mit internen Teams und Abteilungen zusammenarbeiten.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWährend deiner ersten Wochen bei Polestar lernst Du dein Team, die Rolle und den „Polestar Way“ kennen. Danach knüpfen wir mit einem Trainings- und Development-Programm an, das dir fortlaufend neue Möglichkeiten zum Lernen und der Erweiterung deiner Fähigkeiten bietet – wir leben eine positive und wertschätzende Coaching- und Feedbackkultur für alle Polestar-MitarbeiterInnen.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDer ideale Kandidat\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWir suchen jemanden, der immer ein offenes Ohr für unsere KundInnen hat und motiviert ist, einen erstklassigen Service zu bieten. Dabei geben wir dir alle Werkzeuge an die Hand, die Du brauchst, um in deiner Rolle als Customer Engagement Advisor erfolgreich zu sein.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDer beste Hinweis darauf, ob dir dieser Job gefallen wird? Du zeichnest dich durch hervorragende Kommunikationsfähigkeiten aus, indem du in der Lage bist die Fragen unserer KundInnen auf den Punkt zu beantworten. Du bist wortgewandt und kannst unseren KundInnen unser Markenerlebnis näher bringen. Du verfügst über eine flexible und praktische Einstellung, um Lösungen zu finden und bleibst dank deines guten Zeitmanagements auch in hektischen Situationen ruhig. In unserer Arbeitsweise, in der wir Wert auf Selbstorganisation legen, sind Kooperation und Kommunikation wesentliche Fähigkeiten.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDarüber hinaus bringst du folgende Qualifikationen mit:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eKaufmännische oder technische Berufsausbildung oder Studium.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAusgezeichnete Kommunikationsfähigkeiten (mündlich und schriftlich) in Deutsch und gute Kenntnisse der englischen Sprache. Französisch oder Italienisch sind ebenfalls willkommen aber kein Muss.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eErfahrung im Kundenservice oder Vertrieb mit Fokus auf Beantwortung von Anrufen, E-Mails, Tickets oder Erfahrungen im täglichen Kundenkontakt.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eGute Auffassungsgabe, um dich schnell in neue Systeme \u0026amp; Prozesse einarbeiten zu können.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eTeamorientierte Arbeitsweise.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eFließende Deutsch- und Englischkenntnisse (mindestens C1 in Wort und Schrift), die Hauptkommunikation findet auf Deutsch statt\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eFührerschein (Klasse B)\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eImmatrikulation in einem Bachelor- oder Masterstudiengang\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar ist ein internationales Unternehmen, in dem Menschen unterschiedlicher Herkunft zusammenarbeiten.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWir sind auf der ganzen Welt präsent und haben uns den Wachstumsgedanken bewahrt, weshalb Veränderungen bei Polestar an der Tagesordnung sind. Aber das gilt auch für den Fortschritt. Du kannst dich auf ein spannendes und aufregendes Umfeld freuen.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDer Prozess\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWenn die oben genannten Punkte auf dich zutreffen, solltest du dich unbedingt bewerben. Unser Auswahlverfahren ist noch nicht abgeschlossen und die Stelle wird so lange ausgeschrieben, bis sie besetzt ist.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","_jobposting":{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Werkstudent I Customer Engagement Advisor | Germany","description":"\u003cp\u003eWerkstudent I Customer Engagement Advisor | Germany\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDie Möglichkeit\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWir suchen einen Werkstudenten (m/w) für 20 Stunden pro Woche, der in unserem Customer Engagement Center\u003cspan\u003e, der in unserem Customer Engagement Center nachhaltige Beziehungen zu unseren KundInnen aufbaut. Du solltest dich für Elektromobilität und neue Technologien begeistern und den Wunsch haben, die notwendigen Veränderungen herbeizuführen, um das Unternehmen Polestar weiter zu stärken.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDer Arbeitsplatz befindet sich in unserem Büro in Köln. Wir glauben an ein hybrides Modell, wenn es um Remote- und Arbeit vor Ort geht, da wir wissen, dass sowohl persönliche Zusammenarbeit als auch individuelle Zeit notwendig sind, um effizient zu arbeiten.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDie Verantwortung\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAls Teil unseres Customer Engagement Teams arbeitest du direkt mit Kunden sowie mit unseren Partnern zusammen, um gemeinsam hervorragende Kundenerlebnisse zu schaffen. Als Customer Engagement Advisor spielst du eine Schlüsselrolle bei der Betreuung von Interessenten und Kunden während der gesamten Customer Journey.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eZu deinen Aufgaben gehören folgende Tätigkeiten:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eKommunikation per Telefon, Chat und E-Mail sowie Bearbeitung von Informationsanfragen über die Website. Wir haben eine Mischung aus Inbound- und Outbound-Kommunikation, mit dem Schwerpunkt auf Kundenservice und Unterstützung im Bestellprozess.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eBeratung und Begleitung potenzieller Kunden durch den Online-Bestellprozess ihres Polestar.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eProblemlösung für potenzielle und bestehende Kunden.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eUm unseren Kunden ein reibungsloses Erlebnis zu bieten, wirst du eng mit internen Teams und Abteilungen zusammenarbeiten.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWährend deiner ersten Wochen bei Polestar lernst Du dein Team, die Rolle und den „Polestar Way“ kennen. Danach knüpfen wir mit einem Trainings- und Development-Programm an, das dir fortlaufend neue Möglichkeiten zum Lernen und der Erweiterung deiner Fähigkeiten bietet – wir leben eine positive und wertschätzende Coaching- und Feedbackkultur für alle Polestar-MitarbeiterInnen.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDer ideale Kandidat\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWir suchen jemanden, der immer ein offenes Ohr für unsere KundInnen hat und motiviert ist, einen erstklassigen Service zu bieten. Dabei geben wir dir alle Werkzeuge an die Hand, die Du brauchst, um in deiner Rolle als Customer Engagement Advisor erfolgreich zu sein.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"MsoNormal\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eDer beste Hinweis darauf, ob dir dieser Job gefallen wird? Du zeichnest dich durch hervorragende Kommunikationsfähigkeiten aus, indem du in der Lage bist die Fragen unserer KundInnen auf den Punkt zu beantworten. Du bist wortgewandt und kannst unseren KundInnen unser Markenerlebnis näher bringen. Du verfügst über eine flexible und praktische Einstellung, um Lösungen zu finden und bleibst dank deines guten Zeitmanagements auch in hektischen Situationen ruhig. In unserer Arbeitsweise, in der wir Wert auf Selbstorganisation legen, sind Kooperation und Kommunikation wesentliche Fähigkeiten.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDarüber hinaus bringst du folgende Qualifikationen mit:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eKaufmännische oder technische Berufsausbildung oder Studium.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAusgezeichnete Kommunikationsfähigkeiten (mündlich und schriftlich) in Deutsch und gute Kenntnisse der englischen Sprache. Französisch oder Italienisch sind ebenfalls willkommen aber kein Muss.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eErfahrung im Kundenservice oder Vertrieb mit Fokus auf Beantwortung von Anrufen, E-Mails, Tickets oder Erfahrungen im täglichen Kundenkontakt.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eGute Auffassungsgabe, um dich schnell in neue Systeme \u0026amp; Prozesse einarbeiten zu können.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eTeamorientierte Arbeitsweise.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eFließende Deutsch- und Englischkenntnisse (mindestens C1 in Wort und Schrift), die Hauptkommunikation findet auf Deutsch statt\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eFührerschein (Klasse B)\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eImmatrikulation in einem Bachelor- oder Masterstudiengang\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003ePolestar ist ein internationales Unternehmen, in dem Menschen unterschiedlicher Herkunft zusammenarbeiten.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWir sind auf der ganzen Welt präsent und haben uns den Wachstumsgedanken bewahrt, weshalb Veränderungen bei Polestar an der Tagesordnung sind. Aber das gilt auch für den Fortschritt. Du kannst dich auf ein spannendes und aufregendes Umfeld freuen.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDer Prozess\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWenn die oben genannten Punkte auf dich zutreffen, solltest du dich unbedingt bewerben. Unser Auswahlverfahren ist noch nicht abgeschlossen und die Stelle wird so lange ausgeschrieben, bis sie besetzt ist.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polestar journey is an electric one.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Polestar","value":4800529},"datePosted":"2024-08-06T10:13:04+02:00","hiringOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Polestar","sameAs":"https://polestar.teamtailor.com"},"jobLocation":[{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":null,"addressLocality":"Cologne","postalCode":"50667","addressCountry":"DE","addressRegion":"Central Europe"}}]}}]}